ion 10ml.", "manufacturer": "Novartis Consumer Health S.A."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Children aged 6 to 12 years: Instill 1 to 2 drops into each nostril, 1 to 2 times daily. Do not exceed 2 applications per 24 hours. Should not be used for more than 5 consecutive days without medical supervision. It is recommended to administer the final dose of the day immediately before bedtime.", "administration": "Clean the nasal passages before use. Prior to administration, test the dropper ampoule to ensure controlled dosage. Tilt the head backward or lie down on a bed with the head tilted to one side. Instill the drops into each nostril and keep the head tilted back for a short period. Clean and dry the dropper thoroughly before replacing it in the bottle. Each bottle of medication should be used by a single patient only."}, "generalDescription": "Otrivin 0.05% Nasal Drops, manufactured by GSK Consumer Healthcare S.A., are indicated for the treatment of nasal congestion caused by various conditions, assisting in the drainage of secretions from damaged sinus areas, supporting the treatment of nasopharyngeal congestion in otitis media, and facilitating nasal endoscopic examinations.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Sodium dihydrogen phosphate dihydrate, disodium phosphate dodecahydrate, disodium edetate, benzalkonium chloride, sorbitol solution 70%, methylhydroxypropyl cellulose 4000, sodium chloride, purified water.", "activeIngredients": "Xylometazoline hydrochloride 0.05%"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Use with caution and only under the direct guidance of a healthcare professional.", "pediatric": "Contraindicated in children under 6 years of age. Children aged 6°12 years should use the prescribed dosage.", "pregnancy": "Use with caution; avoid excessive use due to the potential risk of systemic vasoconstrictive effects."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Use with caution in patients who exhibit strong reactions to adrenergic active substances (manifesting as insomnia, dizziness, tremor, cardiac arrhythmias, or hypertension).", "Exercise caution in patients with hypertension, cardiovascular disease, hyperthyroidism, diabetes mellitus, pheochromocytoma, or prostatic hyperplasia.", "Contraindicated in patients currently taking or who have taken MAOIs within the past two weeks.", "Prolonged or continuous use exceeding 1 week is not recommended, as it may induce rebound nasal mucosal congestion (rhinitis medicamentosa) and/or atrophic rhinitis.", "Children aged 2 to 11 years must use this product under adult supervision."], "adverseReactionManagement": "If adverse reactions occur, discontinue use immediately and inform a physician or report to the nearest medical facility for prompt management."}	f	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:48:33.832	otrivin-0-05percent-nasal-drops-for-nasal-congestion-sinusitis-and-allergic-rhinitis-10ml-bottle	120
