s": {"activeIngredients": "Itraconazole (as itraconazole microgranules 22%) 100 mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Breastfeeding is not recommended during treatment with itraconazole due to excretion into breast milk.", "pregnancy": "Should only be administered during pregnancy if the potential clinical benefits clearly outweigh the potential fetal risks. Strictly contraindicated in pregnant women or women planning conception."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Use with extreme caution in patients with evidence of ventricular dysfunction, congestive heart failure (CHF), or a history of CHF; therapy must be immediately discontinued if signs or symptoms of heart failure develop during treatment.", "Exercise caution in patients with elevated serum transaminases, chronic liver disease, or a history of drug-induced hepatotoxicity, unless the anticipated therapeutic benefit outweighs the potential risk. Regular hepatic function monitoring is mandatory, especially for patients requiring continuous treatment exceeding one month.", "Discontinue treatment immediately if peripheral neuropathy attributable to itraconazole occurs.", "Appropriate baseline sensitivity testing should be performed prior to initiating systemic treatment for deep-seated fungal infections.", "Itranstad contains sucrose. Patients with rare hereditary disorders of fructose intolerance, glucose-galactose malabsorption, or sucrase-isomaltase insufficiency should not take this medication."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:19:13.453	itranstad-itraconazole-100mg-capsules-for-fungal-infections-1-blister-x-6-capsules	39
