mg losartan/25mg hydrochlorothiazide daily. Dosage adjustments should be individualized based on clinical response and blood pressure targets.", "missedDose": "Take the missed dose as soon as remembered. If it is almost time for the next scheduled dose, omit the missed dose entirely and resume the normal dosing schedule. Do not take a double dose to make up for a forgotten dose.", "administration": "Administer orally as a single daily dose, with or without food.", "overdoseManagement": "Discontinue medication immediately and institute intensive supportive medical care. Manifestations of overdosage may include profound hypotension, tachycardia, or bradycardia due to vagal stimulation. If ingestion is recent, employ emesis or gastric lavage. Monitor vital signs, fluid balance, and electrolyte status closely, treating dehydration, electrolyte imbalances, and hypotension with standard clinical protocols."}, "generalDescription": "Hyzaar 50mg/12.5mg Tablets are a prescription combination formulation comprising an angiotensin II receptor blocker (ARB) and a thiazide diuretic, designed for once-daily administration in the management of hypertension and associated cardiovascular risk reduction.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Microcrystalline cellulose, anhydrous lactose, pregelatinized maize starch, hydroxypropyl cellulose, magnesium stearate, hypromellose, titanium dioxide, quinoline yellow aluminum lake, carnauba wax, and potassium content (4.24 mg / 0.108 mEq per tablet)", "activeIngredients": "Losartan Potassium 50 mg and Hydrochlorothiazide 12.5 mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "No initial dosage adjustment is strictly required based on age alone, though upward titration should proceed with caution in geriatric patients.", "lactation": "Because of the potential for adverse effects on the nursing infant, a decision should be made whether to discontinue nursing or discontinue the drug, taking into account the importance of the drug to the mother.", "