facturingInfo": {"origin": "India", "storage": "Store in a cool, dry place protected from light, at temperatures not exceeding 30°C.", "packaging": "Box of 10 blister packs x 10 tablets", "manufacturer": "TORRENT PHARMACEUTICALS"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Individualized dosage titration is required based on clinical response and disease severity. Epilepsy: Adults and pediatric patients >12 years: Initially 100 mg twice daily, increased gradually by 200 mg/day at weekly intervals. Children 6°12 years: 20°30 mg/kg/day administered in 3 to 4 divided doses. Trigeminal Neuralgia: Initially 100 mg twice daily, titrated upward by 100 mg every 12 hours as clinically indicated. Prophylaxis of Manic-Depressive Psychosis: Initially 400 mg/day in divided doses, titrated gradually until optimal symptom control is achieved.", "missedDose": "Administer the missed dose as soon as remembered. If it is nearly time for the subsequent scheduled dose, omit the missed dose and resume the standard dosing regimen. Do not administer a double dose to compensate for a missed dose.", "administration": "Oral administration via tablets.", "overdoseManagement": "Clinical Manifestations: Neuromuscular abnormalities, cardiovascular complications, respiratory rhythm irregularities, respiratory collapse, deep coma, seizures, motor restlessness, myoclonus, and tremors. Management: Perform immediate gastric lavage; there is no specific antidote available. Hemodialysis is indicated in severe poisoning complicated by renal failure. Fluid resuscitation and supportive care should be administered in young children."}, "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Carbamazepine 200mg"}}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:25:09.228	carbatol-200-carbamazepine-200mg-tablets-for-seizure-disorders-and-neuropathic-pain-box-of-100	316
