vere agitation, tremor, myoclonus, hyperthermia, potentially fatal outcomes."}, {"drug": "QT-prolonging drugs", "effect": "Concomitant use is strictly contraindicated due to the compounded risk of life-threatening cardiac arrhythmias."}, {"drug": "Pimozide", "effect": "Marked increase in QT interval duration; concomitant administration is contraindicated."}, {"drug": "Lithium and tryptophan", "effect": "Potentiation of pharmacodynamic effects; clinical caution and routine monitoring of serum lithium levels are required."}, {"drug": "Serotonergic drugs (Sumatriptan, tramadol, etc.)", "effect": "Elevation of central 5-hydroxytryptamine (5-HT) related effects; concomitant use is not recommended."}, {"drug": "St. John's Wort", "effect": "Heightened incidence of pharmacodynamic adverse events and serotonin toxicity."}, {"drug": "Anticoagulants, NSAIDs", "effect": "Elevated risk of upper gastrointestinal bleeding and systemic hemorrhage."}, {"drug": "Cimetidine", "effect": "Elevated steady-state plasma concentrations of citalopram secondary to hepatic enzyme inhibition."}, {"drug": "CYP2C19 inhibitors (Omeprazole, esomeprazole, etc.)", "effect": "Increased systemic exposure to citalopram; clinical vigilance and dosage reduction may be warranted."}], "effectsOnDriving": "Citalopram exerts minor to moderate influence on the patient's capacity to drive and operate heavy machinery. The drug may impair cognitive judgment, motor reflexes, and emergency response times.", "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity to any active ingredient or excipient component of the medicinal product.", "Concomitant administration with linezolid unless under close clinical monitoring and systemic blood pressure surveillance.", "Patients with baseline QT interval prolongation or congenital long QT syndrome.", "Concomitant use with other medicinal products known to prolong the QT interval.", "Patients currently undergoing treatment with monoamine oxidase inhibitors (MAOIs)."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Stella", "storage": "Store in a dry, cool environment, protected from direct light, at temperatures not exceeding 30°C (86°F). Keep securely out of reach of children.", "packaging": "Box of 3 blister packs x 10 tablets", "manufacturer": "Stella"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults: Major Depressive Disorder: Initiated at 20 mg/day, with a maximum recommended dose of 40 mg/day. Panic Disorder: 10 mg/day for the initial week, subsequently titrated to 20 mg/day, up to a maximum of 40 mg/day. Geriatric Patients (> 65 years): Administer half of the standard recommended adult dose. Hepatic Impairment: Initial dose of 10 mg/day for the first 2 weeks, not to exceed 20 mg/day. Renal Impairment: No dosage adjustment required for mild-to-moderate renal impairment; contraindicated in severe renal impairment. Poor CYP2C19 Metabolizers: Initial dose of 10 mg/day for the first 2 weeks, with a maximum threshold of 20 mg/day.", "missedDose": "Administer the missed dose as soon as remembered. If the scheduled time for the subsequent dose is near, omit the missed dose and resume the standard therapeutic dosing schedule. Do not take a double dose to compensate for a forgotten administration.", "administration": "Citalopram is administered orally as a single daily dose, either in the morning or evening. The tablets should be swallowed whole with adequate water, independently of food intake.", "overdoseManagement": "[object Object]"}, "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Citalopram 20mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Dosage must be reduced by half relative to the standard adult therapeutic regimen.", "lactation": "Use with extreme clinical caution, as citalopram is excreted into human breast milk.", "pediatric": "Contraindicated for use in children and adolescents under 18 years of age.", "pregnancy": "Should not be administered during pregnancy unless clinically mandatory, following a rigorous benefit-risk appraisal by the clinician."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Patients with diabetes mellitus (may alter glycemic homeostasis and insulin requirements).", "Patients with a lowered seizure threshold or underlying seizure disorders.", "Patients at elevated risk for QT interval prolongation, bradycardia, acute myocardial infarction, or decompensated heart failure.", "Geriatric patients and patients with compromised renal or hepatic function.", "Pediatric population and adolescents under 18 years of age.", "Patients being treated for panic disorder (may experience paradoxical intensification of anxiety early in the therapeutic course).", "Heightened risk of hyponatremia and syndrome of inappropriate antidiuretic hormone secretion (SIADH), particularly in elderly female patients.", "Potential risk of emergent suicidal ideation and clinical worsening.", "Patients diagnosed with bipolar disorder.", "Patients with narrow-angle glaucoma or an active ocular medical history.", "Patients with rare hereditary disorders of galactose intolerance, Lapp lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Promptly report any persistent or severe adverse drug reactions encountered during pharmacotherapy to the attending physician or clinical specialist."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:25:52.153	citalopram-20mg-tablets-stella-for-major-depressive-disorder-and-panic-disorder-box-of-3-blister	39
