phamide, Doxorubicin, Bleomycin, Procarbazine, Mechlorethamine", "effect": "Exacerbation of bone marrow suppression."}, {"drug": "Ciclosporin", "effect": "Elevated plasma concentrations."}], "effectsOnDriving": "This medication may cause somnolence, loss of balance, dizziness, and ataxia. Patients should avoid driving or operating machinery while taking this drug.", "contraindications": ["Pregnancy and lactation.", "Known hypersensitivity to Allopurinol.", "Concomitant administration with xanturic agents.", "During an acute gout attack."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Domesco.", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store below 30°C, protect from direct light.", "packaging": "Bottle of 100 tablets.", "manufacturer": "Domesco"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Gout, hyperuricemia: Adults: 100 mg daily, may be gradually increased to 200°400 mg daily, divided into 2°4 doses. Severe cases may require 600°800 mg daily.\\nNeoplastic conditions: 600°800 mg daily, in courses of 2°3 days.\\nPsoriasis: 100°400 mg daily, divided into 3°4 doses.\\nPediatric patients aged 6°15 years: 100 mg per dose, 3 times daily.\\nPediatric patients under 6 years: 50 mg per dose, 3 times daily, or 8 mg/kg/day, divided into 3 doses.\\nRenal impairment: 100 mg daily; dose should be increased only if therapeutic response is inadequate. Doses lower than 100 mg daily or 100 mg administered at intervals greater than 1 day for patients with severe renal failure. For hemodialysis patients, the recommended dose is 300°400 mg immediately following dialysis.", "administration": "Administer orally after meals.", "overdoseManagement": "In the event of an overdose, discontinue medication use and contact a physician immediately. Management measures may include symptomatic treatment and supportive care for vital organ functions."}, "generalDescription": "Allopurinol 300mg is a medication primarily used to manage chronic gout and nephrolithiasis. Gout is characterized by hyperuricemia resulting in the precipitation of urate crystals within joint spaces, precipitating acute inflammatory arthritis. Allopurinol functions as a xanthine oxidase inhibitor, decreasing endogenous uric acid biosynthesis to mitigate recurrent gout attacks and uric acid nephropathy. It is also indicated for hyperuricemia secondary to oncologic conditions, including chemotherapy or radiation therapy.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Lactose, Starch 1500, Povidone, Sunset Yellow lake, Croscarmellose sodium, Aerosil, q.s. one tablet.", "activeIngredients": "Allopurinol 300mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Pregnant and lactating women should not use Allopurinol unless strictly necessary and explicitly directed by a physician.", "pregnancy": "Pregnant and lactating women should not use Allopurinol unless strictly necessary and explicitly directed by a physician."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Discontinue use and notify a physician immediately if signs of skin rash, dysuria, hematuria, ocular irritation, or swelling of the lips or mouth occur."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:15:53.073	allopurinol-300mg-tablets-for-chronic-gout-and-urolithiasis-bottle-of-100-tablets	61
