arly as possible after the onset of a migraine attack.", "overdoseManagement": "Oral doses exceeding 400 mg have not produced adverse effects other than those mentioned. If overdose occurs, monitor patient for at least 10 hours and apply standard supportive treatment as required."}, "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Sumatriptan (as Sumatriptan succinate) 50mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Sumatriptan is excreted into human milk; do not use during breastfeeding.", "pregnancy": "No controlled studies in pregnant women; use only if potential benefit outweighs fetal risk."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Use sumatriptan only when a clear diagnosis of migraine has been established.", "Prior cardiovascular evaluation is recommended before prescribing to patients with risk factors for coronary artery disease.", "Perform appropriate investigations if chest or throat tightness/pain occurs after administration.", "Use with caution in controlled hypertensive patients, patients with hepatic/renal impairment, or history of epilepsy.", "Do not use for atypical headaches that may indicate serious intracranial conditions (e.g., stroke, intracranial hemorrhage).", "Sumatriptan may occasionally cause shock or anaphylactic reactions."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Inform physician of any adverse reactions encountered during drug use."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:36:21.064	sutagran-50mg-film-coated-tablets-for-acute-treatment-of-migraine-attacks-2-blisters-x-6-tablets	\N
