oavailability approaches 100%. Absorption kinetics remain consistent during chronic administration. The apparent volume of distribution (Vd) is approximately 0.6 L/kg, indicating extensive extracellular distribution.", "metabolism": "Piracetam undergoes negligible hepatic biotransformation and exhibits minimal to no binding to plasma proteins.", "elimination": "Renally eliminated entirely as unchanged parent drug. Renal clearance in subjects with normal renal function is approximately 86 mL/min; over 95% of the systemic dose is recovered in urine within 30 hours post-dose. Plasma elimination half-life is 4 to 5 hours, while cerebrospinal fluid elimination half-life ranges from 6 to 8 hours. In patients with severe, irreversible renal impairment, elimination half-life is markedly prolonged up to 48 to 50 hours."}, "manufacturingInfo": {"storage": "Store in a dry location at controlled room temperatures not exceeding 30°C, protected from direct light and moisture."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Standard adult dosage ranges from 30 to 160 mg/kg/day, administered in 2 to 4 divided doses. In severe clinical conditions, dosages may be escalated up to 12 g/day. Management of chronic alcoholism: 12 g/day during acute withdrawal, tapered to 2.4 g/day for maintenance. Cognitive impairment secondary to head trauma: 9 to 12 g/day initially, maintenance dose of 2.4 g/day. Sickle cell anemia: 180 mg/kg/day divided into 4 equal doses. Treatment of cortical myoclonus: Initial dose of 7.2 g/day, titrated upward by 4.8 g/day every 3 to 4 days up to a maximum threshold of 20 g/day.", "missedDose": "Administer the missed dose as soon as remembered. If it is nearly time for the subsequent scheduled administration, omit the missed dose and resume the standard dosing schedule. Do not administer a double dose to compensate for a forgotten administration.", "administration": "Administered via slow intravenous injection, continuous intravenous infusion, or deep intramuscular injection. 