1550	Breztri Aerosphere 160/7.2/5mcg AstraZeneca Inhalation Aerosol for Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (120 Metered Actuations)	P28052	\N	\N	AstraZeneca	France	1527778.00	1100000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/product/20240807084414-0-P28052_1.jpg	Breztri Aerosphere 160/7.2/5mcg is a fixed-dose triple combination inhalation aerosol containing budesonide, glycopyrronium, and formoterol fumarate dihydrate, indicated for the maintenance treatment of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) in adults.	{"indications": ["For the maintenance treatment of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) in adults."], "sideEffects": ["Pneumonia", "Headache", "Urinary tract infection"], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Strong Cytochrom P450 3A4 inhibitors (e.g., Ketoconazole, Ritonavir, Atazanavir, Clarithromycin, Indinavir, Itraconazole, Nefazodone, Nelfinavir, Saquinavir, Telithromycin)", "effect": "May inhibit metabolism and increase systemic exposure of budesonide. Use with caution during co-administration."}, {"drug": "Adrenergic stimulants", "effect": "The sympathetic agonist effects of formoterol may be potentiated. Use with caution when administered concurrently."}, {"drug": "Xanthine derivatives, steroids, or diuretics", "effect": "May potentiate the hypokalemic effect of beta2-adrenergic agonist medications."}, {"drug": "Non-potassium-sparing diuretics", "effect": "Hypokalemia and/or ECG changes may be exacerbated."}, {"drug": "Monoamine oxidase inhibitors, tricyclic antidepressants, QTc-prolonging agents", "effect": "Cardiovascular effects of adrenergic agonists may be potentiated. May increase the risk of ventricular arrhythmias."}, {"drug": "Beta-adrenergic receptor blocking agents", "effect": "May weaken or antagonize the effect of each other. Beta-blockers may induce severe bronchospasm in patients with COPD."}, {"drug": "Anticholinergic medications", "effect": "Potential for additive anticholinergic effects. Avoid concurrent administration with other medications containing anticholinergic components."}], "effectsOnDriving": "Breztri Aerosphere has no or negligible influence on the ability to drive and use machines. However, dizziness is an uncommon adverse reaction that should be taken into consideration.", "contraindications": ["Breztri Aerosphere is contraindicated in patients with hypersensitivity to budesonide, glycopyrrolate, formoterol, or any of the excipients."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "United Kingdom", "origin": "France", "storage": "Do not store above 30°C. Do not expose to temperatures higher than 50°C. Do not puncture the container. Store in a dry place. Use within 3 months after opening the foil pouch.", "packaging": "Box containing 1 foil pouch with 1 pressurized metered-dose inhaler (120 metered actuations)", "manufacturer": "AstraZeneca Dunkerque Production"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "The recommended dose is two inhalations twice daily (in the morning and in the evening). Do not use more than two inhalations twice daily.", "missedDose": "Administer the missed dose as soon as remembered. If it is almost time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and resume the regular dosing schedule. Do not double the dose to make up for a forgotten dose.", "administration": "Prime Breztri Aerosphere prior to first use by releasing 4 actuations into the air away from the face, shaking well before each actuation. If the inhaler has not been used for more than 7 days, has been dropped, or after weekly cleaning, re-prime the inhaler by releasing 2 actuations into the air away from the face, shaking well before each actuation. The canister is equipped with a dose counter. Rinse the mouth with water after inhalation without swallowing.", "overdoseManagement": "There is no clinical report of overdosage with Breztri Aerosphere. Risks associated with overdosage for each individual component apply to Breztri Aerosphere. Management includes discontinuation of Breztri Aerosphere, symptomatic treatment, and/or supportive care. Cardioselective beta-blockers may be considered, but with extreme caution due to the risk of inducing bronchospasm. Cardiovascular monitoring is recommended. Budesonide overdosage may cause hyperadrenocorticism. Glycopyrrolate overdosage may manifest as anticholinergic signs such as nausea, vomiting, dizziness, blurred vision, increased intraocular pressure, severe constipation, or urinary retention. Formoterol fumarate overdosage may cause seizures, angina, hypertension, hypotension, tachycardia, arrhythmia, nervousness, headache, tremor, muscle cramps, nausea, dizziness, sleep disturbances, metabolic acidosis, hyperglycemia, and hypokalemia. Cardiac arrest and death may be associated with formoterol fumarate overdosage."}, "generalDescription": "Breztri Aerosphere is a triple-combination inhalation medication containing budesonide (an inhaled corticosteroid - ICS), glycopyrrolate (a long-acting muscarinic antagonist - LAMA), and formoterol fumarate dihydrate (a long-acting beta2-adrenergic agonist - LABA). The medication is indicated for the maintenance treatment of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) in adults.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Excipients q.s.", "activeIngredients": "Budesonide 160mcg, Glycopyrronium 7.2mcg, Formoterol fumarate dihydrate 5mcg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "No dosage adjustment is required in elderly patients, though heightened sensitivity in certain older individuals cannot be ruled out.", "lactation": "There is no available data on the excretion of Breztri Aerosphere into human breast milk or its effects on breastfed infants. Balance the therapeutic benefits against potential risks.", "pediatric": "Breztri Aerosphere is not indicated for use in pediatric patients.", "pregnancy": "There are no adequate and well-controlled clinical studies of Breztri Aerosphere in pregnant women. Use only if the potential benefit justifies the potential risk to the fetus."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Serious asthma-related events - hospitalizations, endotracheal intubation, death: Breztri Aerosphere is not indicated for the treatment of asthma.", "Deterioration of disease and acute episodes: Initiation of treatment with Breztri Aerosphere in rapidly deteriorating or life-threatening COPD is not recommended. It should not be used as a rescue medication for acute symptom relief.", "Avoid excessive use of Breztri Aerosphere and do not co-administer with other long-acting beta2-adrenergic agonists.", "Oropharyngeal candidiasis: Patients should rinse their mouth with water without swallowing after inhalation. Appropriate antifungal therapy should be instituted if candidiasis develops.", "Pneumonia: Healthcare providers should remain vigilant for the possible development of pneumonia in patients with COPD.", "Immunosuppression and infection risk: Patients using immunosuppressive drugs are more susceptible to infections.", "Transfer of patients from systemic corticosteroid therapy: Special care is needed for patients transitioning from systemic corticosteroids to ICS due to reported fatalities resulting from adrenal insufficiency.", "Re-emergence of allergic conditions previously controlled by systemic corticosteroids.", "Corticosteroid withdrawal syndrome.", "Hyperadrenocorticism and adrenal suppression.", "Drug interactions with potent Cytochrome P450 3A4 inhibitors.", "Paradoxical bronchospasm: May induce paradoxical bronchospasm; discontinue the medication immediately and institute alternative therapy with a short-acting bronchodilator.", "Hypersensitivity reactions including anaphylaxis: Discontinue Breztri Aerosphere immediately if signs of allergic reactions occur.", "Cardiovascular effects: May cause increases in pulse rate, blood pressure, and cardiac arrhythmias. Use with caution in patients with cardiovascular disorders.", "Bone mineral density reduction: Reductions in bone mineral density (BMD) have been observed with long-term administration of medications containing ICS.", "Increased intraocular pressure, cataracts, and worsening of narrow-angle glaucoma: Use with caution in patients with narrow-angle glaucoma.", "Worsening of urinary retention: Exercise caution when administering Breztri Aerosphere to patients with urinary retention.", "Concomitant conditions: Exercise caution when administering Breztri Aerosphere to patients with seizure disorders or thyrotoxicosis.", "Hypokalemia and hyperglycemia: Beta-adrenergic agonists may produce significant hypokalemia and transient hyperglycemia."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:42:09.16	breztri-aerosphere-160-7-2-5mcg-astrazeneca-inhalation-aerosol-for-chronic-obstructive-pulmonary	147
