a attacks.,Patients using bronchodilators by inhalation are advised to use the bronchodilator prior to Pulmicort administration to enhance the penetration of the medication into the bronchial tree. An adequate time interval should be maintained between the two inhalations.,Pulmicort Respules should be administered using a suitable jet nebulizer.,Prior to use, gently agitate the single-dose ampoule by swirling to resuspend the contents evenly.,Hold the single-dose ampoule upright and open it by twisting off the top tab (wing).,Place the open end of the ampoule firmly into the nebulizer reservoir and squeeze slowly. Single-dose ampoules are marked with a fill line (applicable only to Pulmicort 0.25 mg/mL and 0.5 mg/mL respules). This line indicates a volume of 1 mL when the ampoule is inverted.,If only 1 mL is to be used, express the contents until the liquid level reaches the indicated fill line.,Protect opened ampoules from light. An opened ampoule must be used within 12 hours. Note that if only 1 mL is used, sterility of the remaining volume cannot be guaranteed.,Prior to using the remaining liquid, gently swirl the ampoule to resuspend the contents. Sedimentation may occur during storage of Pulmicort Respules. If the medication does not return to a uniform suspension after agitation, discard the ampoule.,Rinse the mouth thoroughly with water after each nebulization to minimize the risk of oral candidiasis.,If a face mask is used, ensure the mask fits snugly during nebulization. Wash the face thoroughly after each treatment session.,The nebulizer chamber, mouthpiece, or face mask must be cleaned after every use. Wash all parts in warm water using a mild detergent or according to the manufacturer's instructions provided with the nebulizer system. Rinse thoroughly and dry by connecting the nebulizer chamber to the compressor or air supply."}, "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Budesonide 1 mg per 2 mL"}}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:43:09.348	pulmicort-1mg-2ml-b