e dose to make up for a forgotten dose.", "administration": "For oral administration. Swallow capsules whole; do not chew or open the capsule, as contact with the capsule contents can result in irritation of the oro-pharyngeal mucosa. Can be taken with or without food.", "overdoseManagement": "No specific antidote is available. In case of suspected overdose, provide symptomatic treatment and institute appropriate supportive measures."}, "generalDescription": "Avodart is a soft capsule containing the active ingredient dutasteride, indicated for the treatment and prevention of benign prostatic hyperplasia (BPH) progression by reducing symptoms, decreasing prostate volume, improving urinary flow, reducing the risk of acute urinary retention (AUR), and lowering the need for BPH-related surgery.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Capsule content: monodiglycerides of caprylic/capric acid, butylated hydroxytoluene. Capsule shell: gelatin, glycerol, titanium dioxide (E171, CI 77891), yellow iron oxide (E172, CI 77492). Capsule lubricants: medium-chain triglycerides and lecithin.", "activeIngredients": "Dutasteride 0.5mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "No dosage adjustment required.", "lactation": "It is unknown whether the medication is excreted in human milk. Weigh the benefits versus risks carefully.", "pediatric": "Contraindicated.", "pregnancy": "Contraindicated. May inhibit the development of external genitalia in male fetuses."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Prostate cancer: Men taking Avodart should be regularly evaluated for prostate cancer risk, including prostate-specific antigen (PSA) testing.", "Prostate-specific antigen (PSA): The medication decreases mean serum PSA levels by approximately 50% after 6 months of treatment.", "Cardiovascular adverse events.", "Male breast cancer: Patients should promptly report any changes in breast tissue such as lumps or nipple discharge.", "Leaking capsules: If contact is made with leaking capsules, the affected