"For intranasal administration only. Prime the pump before initial use, after periods of non-use of several days, or after cleaning. Shake the bottle, blow the nose gently, tilt the head forward, insert the nozzle into the nostril, depress the pump while inhaling through the nose, and exhale through the mouth.", "overdoseManagement": "Prolonged administration of high doses may result in temporary suppression of adrenal function. Treatment should be continued at the effective dose required to control symptoms; adrenal function will recover within a few days."}, "generalDescription": "Flixonase 0.05% Nasal Spray is a topical corticosteroid product indicated for the treatment and prophylaxis of seasonal allergic rhinitis, including pollen-induced allergic rhinitis (hay fever) and perennial allergic rhinitis.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Anhydrous Dextrose, Microcrystalline Cellulose and Carboxymethylcellulose Sodium (Avicel RC591), Phenylethyl Alcohol, Benzalkonium Chloride, Polysorbate 80, Dilute Hydrochloric Acid, Purified Water.", "activeIngredients": "Fluticasone Propionate"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Administer the standard adult dosage.", "lactation": "Use only if the potential benefit outweighs the potential risks to the nursing infant.", "pediatric": "Children aged 4 to 11 years should receive 1 spray per nostril once daily. The lowest effective dose should be maintained to minimize the risk of growth suppression.", "pregnancy": "Use only if the potential benefit justifies the potential risk to the fetus."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Bacterial infections of the nasal passages must be appropriately treated.", "Caution must be exercised when transferring patients from systemic corticosteroid therapy to nasal spray administration.", "Systemic effects should be monitored when high doses are administered over prolonged periods.", "Reduction in growth velocity in children has been reported; the lowest effective dose should be maintained.",