rsensitivity to macrolide antibiotics or any excipients.", "Concomitant administration with astemizole, cisapride, pimozide, or terfenadine.", "Concomitant administration with ergotamine or dihydroergotamine.", "Concomitant administration with HMG-CoA reductase inhibitors (statins) extensively metabolized by CYP3A4 (lovastatin or simvastatin).", "History of QT prolongation on electrocardiogram (ECG) or ventricular cardiac arrhythmia.", "Concomitant use with colchicine in patients with hepatic or renal impairment who are taking P-glycoprotein or CYP3A4 inhibitors."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Abbott", "origin": "United States", "storage": "Store at room temperature (15°30°C). The reconstituted suspension is stable for 14 days; do not refrigerate.", "packaging": "60ml bottle"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Pediatric patients 6 months to 12 years of age: 7.5 mg/kg twice daily (maximum 500 mg per dose). Mycobacterium infections: 15°30 mg/kg/day divided into 2 doses. Patients with renal impairment (creatinine clearance < 30 mL/min): reduce dosage by half.", "missedDose": "Take the missed dose as soon as remembered. If it is almost time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and resume the normal dosing schedule. Do not double the dose.", "administration": "Prepare the oral suspension by adding water to the granules in the bottle and shaking vigorously prior to administration. Can be taken with or without food, and may be administered with milk.", "overdoseManagement": "Symptoms: Nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, diarrhea. Management: Symptomatic and supportive treatment; hemodialysis is not effective."}, "generalDescription": "Klacid 125mg/5ml, manufactured by PT. Abbott Indonesia, is a macrolide antibiotic with Clarithromycin as its primary active ingredient.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Sucrose, xanthan gum, silicon dioxide, potassium sorbate, citric acid, maltodextrin, titanium dioxide, fruit flavoring agents.", "activeIngredients": "Clarithromycin 125mg (per 5ml)"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Special caution is required when co-administered with colchicine due to the risk of toxicity.", "lactation": "Safety has not been established; the drug is excreted in breast milk.", "pediatric": "Dosage is based on body weight (6 months to 12 years of age).", "pregnancy": "Should not be used unless the potential benefit outweighs the potential risk."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Use with caution in patients with severe renal impairment or hepatic impairment.", "Risk of superinfection with non-susceptible bacteria or fungi during prolonged use.", "Risk of Clostridium difficile-associated diarrhea (pseudomembranous colitis).", "May exacerbate myasthenia gravis.", "Exercise caution when administered concomitantly with CYP3A4 inducers, hypoglycemic agents, warfarin, or triazolobenzodiazepines.", "Risk of QT interval prolongation.", "Discontinue medication immediately if severe hypersensitivity reactions occur, such as Stevens-Johnson syndrome or anaphylactic shock."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Discontinue use and notify a physician or proceed to the nearest medical facility for prompt medical management."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:46:59.245	klacid-125mg-5ml-clarithromycin-granules-for-oral-suspension-for-respiratory-tract-infections	3
