: ["Hypersensitivity to any of the ingredients in this medication.", "Patients with glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase (G6PD) deficiency."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "HAU GIANG PHARMACEUTICAL JOINT STOCK COMPANY", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store in a dry place, protected from light, at temperatures below 30°C.", "packaging": "Box of 10 blisters x 10 tablets."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults and adolescents aged 12 years and older: Take 1 tablet 3 to 4 times daily. The dosing interval between doses should be 4 to 6 hours. Do not exceed 6 tablets per day. In patients with severe renal impairment (creatinine clearance < 10 mL/min), the interval between doses must be at least 8 hours.", "missedDose": "Take the dose as soon as remembered. If it is almost time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and resume the normal dosing schedule. Do not double the dose.", "administration": "Hapacol 650 Extra is administered via the oral route.", "overdoseManagement": "Paracetamol overdose: Hepatic necrosis is the most serious acute toxic effect. Management: Gastric lavage within 4 hours, administration of sulfhydryl compounds (N-acetylcysteine) or methionine, activated charcoal, and saline laxatives. Caffeine overdose: Insomnia, restlessness, agitation, and delirium."}, "generalDescription": "Hapacol 650 Extra is manufactured by Hau Giang Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company. Containing Paracetamol and Caffeine as active ingredients, it is a medication used to relieve pain including headaches, migraines, sore throats, dysmenorrhea, toothaches, and muscle aches, and to reduce fever.", "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Paracetamol 650mg, Caffeine 65mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Use this medication only when strictly necessary.", "pregnancy": "Use this medication only when strictly necessary."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Patients with phenylketonuria and those who must restrict phenylalanine intake should avoid using paracetamol concomitantly with medications or foods containing aspartame.", "Hypersensitive individuals (e.g., those with asthma) should avoid paracetamol combined with medications or foods containing sulfites.", "Use with caution in patients with preexisting anemia, or hepatic and renal impairment.", "Avoid or limit alcohol consumption as it increases hepatotoxicity.", "Exercise caution in patients with hypertension when using high doses of caffeine.", "Warning regarding severe cutaneous adverse reactions (SCAR) such as Stevens-Johnson syndrome (SJS), toxic epidermal necrolysis (TEN), Lyell syndrome, and acute generalized exanthematous pustulosis (AGEP)."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Notify your physician immediately of any adverse reactions experienced while using this medication."}	f	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:47:31.896	hapacol-650mg-extra-tablets-for-pain-relief-and-fever-reduction-10-blisters-x-10-tablets	62
