 of children.", "packaging": "Shelf life is 24 months from the manufacturing date."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "For mucolytic treatment: Adults and adolescents over 14 years: 1 sachet 2 - 3 times daily (400 - 600mg Acetylcysteine/day). Children 6-14 years: 1 sachet twice daily (400mg Acetylcysteine/day). Children 2-5 years: 1/2 sachet 2 - 3 times daily (200 - 300mg Acetylcysteine/day). For hypersecretion: Children over 6 years: 1 sachet 3 times daily (600mg Acetylcysteine/day). Children 2 - 5 years: 1 sachet twice daily (400mg Acetylcysteine/day). Patients with hypersecretion weighing over 30kg may receive doses up to 800mg/day if clinically indicated.", "missedDose": "If a dose of ACC 200 is missed or too little was taken, continue taking the medication at the next scheduled time according to the dosage instructions.", "administration": "The medication can be dissolved in water and taken after meals. Chronic bronchitis and hypersecretion require prolonged administration of ACC 200 to achieve prophylactic effects against infection.", "overdoseManagement": "No cases of toxic overdose have been observed with oral Acetylcysteine administration. Symptoms of overdose may include gastrointestinal irritation (nausea, vomiting, diarrhea). Neonates are at risk of hypersecretion severity. Symptomatic treatment should be provided as necessary."}, "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Acetylcysteine 200mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "There is no information on excretion into breast milk. Use only after a careful risk-benefit evaluation by a physician.", "pregnancy": "Data is limited. Use only after a careful risk-benefit evaluation by a physician."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Caution is advised in patients with a history of or active bronchial asthma, or peptic ulcer disease.", "The administration of Acetylcysteine may increase the volume of bronchial secretions. If the patient is unable to expectorate effectively, appropriate postural drainage and aspiration measures should be implemented.", "Very rare reports of severe skin reactions such as Stevens-Johnson syndrome and Lyell's syndrome have been associated with Acetylcysteine. If new skin or mucosal changes occur, discontinue treatment immediately and consult a physician."]}	f	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:50:15.951	acc-200mg-acetylcysteine-mucolytic-powder-for-oral-suspension-for-bronchopulmonary-disorders-box-of	\N
