otentiated."}, {"drug": "Potassium-depleting medications (diuretics, amphotericin B, xanthenes, beta-2 agonists)", "effect": "Increased risk of hypokalemia."}], "effectsOnDriving": "There is currently no evidence regarding the influence of the medication on the ability to drive and operate machinery.", "contraindications": ["Glucocorticoids are contraindicated in patients with Cushing's disease."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Pymepharco", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store in a dry, cool place (below 30°C). Protect from light.", "packaging": "Box of 3 blisters x 10 tablets", "manufacturer": "Pymepharco Joint Stock Company (Vietnam)"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "The initial dosage depends on the specific condition being treated (ranging from 4 mg to 360 mg/day depending on indication). The total recommended daily dosage can be administered as a single dose or divided into multiple doses. For alternate-day therapy, double the minimum daily dose is administered as a single dose every other day at 8:00 AM."}, "generalDescription": "Menison 16mg tablets are anti-inflammatory medications containing the active ingredient methylprednisolone, a potent synthetic corticosteroid. Corticosteroids possess anti-inflammatory, anti-allergic, and immunosuppressive properties. Methylprednisolone is widely used for the treatment of numerous inflammatory conditions, severe allergies, and autoimmune disorders.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Lactose, hydroxypropyl cellulose, microcrystalline cellulose, sodium starch glycolate, magnesium stearate, talc.", "activeIngredients": "Methylprednisolone 16mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Close clinical supervision is necessary due to the increased risk of osteoporosis, hypertension, hypokalemia, diabetes mellitus, susceptibility to bacterial infections, and skin thinning.", "lactation": "Use with caution.", "pediatric": "Carefully monitor growth and development. Pediatric patients may experience growth retardati