ction of other neuromuscular blocking agents."}], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Glenmark", "origin": "India", "storage": "Store below 30°C. Do not freeze. Keep out of reach of children.", "packaging": "Box of 1 tube (15g).", "manufacturer": "Glenmark Pharmaceuticals Ltd."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Apply once daily at bedtime.", "missedDose": "[object Object]", "administration": "Apply a thin film of gel to clean, dry affected areas once daily at bedtime. Avoid simultaneous application of other potentially irritating topical medications. During the initial weeks of therapy, an apparent exacerbation of acne may occur; this is due to the action of the medication on previously unseen microcomedones and should not be considered a reason to discontinue treatment. Therapeutic results are typically observed after 8 to 12 weeks of consistent use.", "overdoseManagement": "KLENZIT-C Gel is intended for external topical use only. Excessive application will not yield faster or better results and may lead to marked redness, peeling, or cutaneous discomfort. The acute oral toxicity of Adapalene in mice and rats is greater than 10 mg/kg. Chronic oral ingestion of Adapalene may lead to systemic side effects similar to those observed with excessive oral vitamin A intake. Topical application of Clindamycin may result in systemic absorption sufficient to produce systemic adverse effects."}, "generalDescription": "Klenzit-C is a topical dermatological gel formulated for the treatment of acne vulgaris, combining two active pharmaceutical ingredients: Adapalene (a retinoid) and Clindamycin Phosphate (a lincosamide antibiotic).", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Disodium edetate, Carbomer 940, Propylene glycol, Methylparaben, Phenoxyethanol, Poloxamer 407, Sodium hydroxide, Purified water q.s.", "activeIngredients": "Each gram of gel contains: Adapalene USP 1 mg, Clindamycin Phosphate USP equivalent to Clindamycin 10 mg."}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Clinical studies of Adapalene did not include sufficient numbers of subjects aged 65 and over to determine whether they respond differently from younger patients. Other reported clinical experience has not identified differences in responses between elderly and younger patients. Furthermore, acne vulgaris is predominantly a condition of adolescence and young adulthood, rendering treatment in geriatric populations generally unnecessary.", "lactation": "[object Object]", "pediatric": "Safety and effectiveness of the Adapalene and Clindamycin combination in pediatric patients below the age of 12 years have not been established; therefore, use in this age group is not recommended.", "pregnancy": "[object Object]"}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Because Adapalene may cause local irritation, concomitant use of other potentially irritating topical products (such as medicated soaps, harsh cleansers, cosmetics with strong drying effects, high-alcohol preparations, astringents, or alkalis) should be approached with caution. Special care must be taken when using preparations containing sulfur, resorcinol, or salicylic acid concurrently with Klenzit-C gel; allow previous treatments to clear before starting therapy. Clindamycin exhibits neuromuscular blocking properties and should be used with caution in patients receiving concurrent neuromuscular blocking agents, as it may potentiate their action."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:50:59.328	klenzit-c-adapalene-0-1percent-and-clindamycin-1percent-w-w-topical-gel-for-acne-vulgaris-15g-tube	258
1740	Rosuvastatin STELLA 10mg Film-Coated Tablets for Hypercholesterolemia (3 Blisters x 10 Tablets)	P02588	\N	\N	Stella Pharm	Vietnam	107059.00	91000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250728082752-0-P02588.png?versionId=e5QHXG1dQVtzzkBIlk6TU8ZP6grkq1v7	Rosuvastatin STELLA 10mg film-coated tablets indicated for the treatment of hypercholesterolemia, packaged in 3 blisters of 10 tablets.	{"sideEffects": ["Endocrine disorders: Diabetes mellitus, hypertension, increased HbA1c.", "Nervous system disorders: Headache, dizziness.", "Gastrointestinal disorders: Constipation, nausea, abdominal pain.", "Musculoskeletal and connective tissue disorders: Myalgia.", "General disorders: Asthenia, cognitive impairment (such as memory loss, confusion, etc.).", "Skin and subcutaneous tissue disorders: Pruritus, rash, and urticaria.", "Immune system disorders: Hypersensitivity reactions including angioedema.", "Gastrointestinal disorders: Pancreatitis.", "Musculoskeletal and connective tissue disorders: Myopathy (including myositis), rhabdomyolysis."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Ciclosporin", "effect": "When ciclosporin is co-administered with rosuvastatin, rosuvastatin AUC values are on average 7 times higher than those seen in healthy volunteers, while plasma concentrations of ciclosporin are unaffected."}, {"drug": "Vitamin K antagonists (such as warfarin or other coumarin anticoagulants)", "effect": "The initiation of treatment or dose escalation of rosuvastatin in patients concomitantly treated with vitamin K antagonists may result in an increase in International Normalized Ratio (INR). Discontinuation or reduction of rosuvastatin may result in a decrease in INR."}, {"drug": "Ezetimibe", "effect": "Concomitant use of rosuvastatin and ezetimibe does not result in a change in AUC or Cmax of either drug. However, a pharmacodynamic interaction, in terms of adverse effects, cannot be ruled out."}, {"drug": "Gemfibrozil and other lipid-lowering medications", "effect": "Concomitant use of rosuvastatin and gemfibrozil results in a 2-fold increase in rosuvastatin Cmax and AUC. The 40 mg dose is contraindicated when combined with fibrates."}, {"drug": "HIV protease inhibitors (atazanavir, atazanavir/ritonavir, and lopinavir/ritonavir)", "effect": "Co-administration with rosuvastatin results in a approximately 3-fold increase in rosuvastatin exposure."}, {"drug": "Antacids", "effect": "Simultaneous dosing of an antacid with rosuvastatin results in a 20% decrease in rosuvastatin AUC and a 30% decrease in Cmax."}, {"drug": "Oral contraceptives / Hormone Replacement Therapy (HRT)", "effect": "Concomitant use of rosuvastatin and an oral contraceptive resulted in an increase in ethinyl estradiol AUC of 26% and norgestrel AUC of 34%."}, {"drug": "Cytochrome P450 enzymes", "effect": "Results from in vitro and in vivo studies show that rosuvastatin is neither an inhibitor nor an inducer of cytochrome P450 enzymes. Furthermore, rosuvastatin is a poor substrate for these isoenzymes. Therefore, pharmacokinetic interactions resulting from enzyme induction or inhibition are unlikely."}], "effectsOnDriving": "Studies to determine the effect of rosuvastatin on the ability to drive and use machines have not been performed. However, based on its pharmacodynamic properties, rosuvastatin is unlikely to affect this ability. When driving vehicles or operating machinery, it should be noted that dizziness may occur during treatment.", "contraindications": ["Patients with hypersensitivity to any component of the medication.", "Patients with active liver disease including unexplained persistent elevations of serum transaminases and any serum transaminase elevation exceeding 3 times the upper limit of normal (ULN).", "Patients with severe renal impairment (creatinine clearance < 30 mL/min).", "Patients with myopathy.", "Pregnant and lactating women, and women of childbearing potential not employing appropriate contraceptive measures."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Stellapharm", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store in a tight container in a dry place. Temperature not exceeding 30°C.", "packaging": "10 tablets per blister. Box of 3 blisters.", "manufacturer": "Stellapharm (Vietnam)"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "The usual starting dose is 5 to 10 mg once daily, depending on plasma cholesterol levels, cardiovascular risk factors, and risk factors for adverse reactions. If necessary, the dose may be adjusted at 4-week intervals to the usual maximum dose of 20 mg once daily. The 40 mg dose may be administered under specialist supervision in patients with severe hypercholesterolemia. Elderly patients, Asian patients, and patients with predisposing factors for myopathy should initiate therapy at 5 mg. Patients taking ciclosporin should be limited to 5 mg once daily, and those taking gemfibrozil or ritonavir-boosted lopinavir should be limited to 10 mg once daily. Patients with severe hypercholesterolemia, such as homozygous familial hypercholesterolemia, may start with 20 mg once daily. Patients with renal impairment (creatinine clearance between 30 and 60 mL/min) should start at 5 mg once daily with a maximum dose of 20 mg once daily. When combined with atazanavir, atazanavir/ritonavir, or lopinavir/ritonavir, rosuvastatin dosage is limited to a maximum of 10 mg once daily. Note: The dosages above are for reference only. Specific dosing depends on the patient's condition and disease progression. Consult a physician or healthcare professional for appropriate dosing.", "missedDose": "Take the missed dose as soon as remembered. However, if it is almost time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and resume the normal dosing schedule. Do not double the dose to make up for a forgotten dose.", "administration": "Rosuvastatin STELLA 10mg is taken orally, as a single dose at any time of the day, with or without food. Patients should be placed on a standard cholesterol-lowering diet before receiving rosuvastatin and should continue this diet during treatment. Dosage may be adjusted carefully based on individual patient needs and therapeutic response by titrating the dose at intervals of no less than 4 weeks. Adverse drug reactions must be closely monitored, particularly adverse musculoskeletal effects.", "overdoseManagement": "There is no specific treatment in the event of an overdose. In the event of overdose, symptomatic treatment and supportive measures should be employed as required. Liver function and creatine kinase levels should be monitored. Hemodialysis is unlikely to be of benefit."}, "generalDescription": "Rosuvastatin STELLA 10mg, manufactured by Stellapharm Joint Venture Co., Ltd. - Branch 1, contains rosuvastatin 10 mg as its active ingredient. It is a lipid-modifying agent, specifically an HMG-CoA reductase inhibitor. The tablets are round, light red, film-coated, scored on one side and plain on the other.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Lactose monohydrate, microcrystalline cellulose, magnesium stearate, crospovidone, anhydrous dibasic calcium phosphate, hypromellose, polyethylene glycol 6000, talc, titanium dioxide, iron oxide red.", "activeIngredients": "Rosuvastatin 10mg (Equivalent to rosuvastatin calcium 10.4mg)"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Elderly patients (> 70 years) have predisposing factors for rhabdomyolysis and require caution.", "lactation": "Contraindicated. Rosuvastatin is excreted in the milk of rats. Data on excretion in human milk are not available.", "pediatric": "[object Object]", "pregnancy": "Contraindicated. Since cholesterol and other products of cholesterol biosynthesis are essential for the development of the fetus, the potential risk from inhibition of HMG-CoA reductase outweighs the advantage of treatment during pregnancy."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Creatine kinase (CK) should be monitored in the following situations: Renal impairment, hypothyroidism, personal or family history of hereditary muscular disorders, previous history of muscular toxicity with another statin or fibrate, history of liver disease and/or substantial alcohol consumption, elderly patients (> 70 years) with predisposing factors for rhabdomyolysis, situations where an increase in plasma concentration may occur, and in special patient populations. If CK levels are significantly elevated (> 5 x ULN) at baseline, statin treatment should not be initiated.", "During statin treatment: Patients should report promptly any unexplained muscle pain, tenderness, or weakness. If these symptoms occur, CK levels should be evaluated for appropriate medical intervention.", "Musculoskeletal effects: Rhabdomyolysis has been reported more frequently in patients receiving rosuvastatin at a 40 mg dose compared to lower doses. Discontinue rosuvastatin if marked elevation of serum CK levels occurs or if myopathy is diagnosed or suspected. Caution should be exercised in patients over 65 years of age, patients with uncontrolled hypothyroidism, and patients with renal impairment. Patients must promptly report any signs or symptoms of muscle pain, fatigue, fever, dark urine, nausea, or vomiting during treatment.", "Hepatic effects: Liver enzymes tests should be performed prior to initiating statin therapy and as clinically indicated thereafter.", "Renal effects: Dose reduction should be considered in patients taking the 40 mg dose who exhibit unexplained persistent proteinuria during routine urinalysis.", "Concomitant use of lipid-lowering statins with medications for HIV and hepatitis C virus (HCV) treatment may increase the risk of muscle injury, most seriously rhabdomyolysis, leading to secondary renal failure and potential fatalities.", "Rosuvastatin STELLA 10mg contains lactose. Patients with rare hereditary problems of galactose intolerance, total lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption should not take this medication."], "adverseReactionManagement": "If experiencing any adverse drug reactions, discontinue use and notify a physician or visit the nearest medical facility for timely management."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:51:16.052	rosuvastatin-stella-10mg-film-coated-tablets-for-hypercholesterolemia-3-blisters-x-10-tablets	39
1743	Pizar 6mg Tablets for Helminthiasis and Onchocerciasis (1 Blister x 4 Tablets)	P02456	\N	\N	Davipharm	Vietnam	241379.00	210000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/product/20251110081651-0-P02456.png?versionId=sefWFu_365TU_.KtM7foUJo2TWTo0HJz	Pizar 6 contains ivermectin, indicated for the treatment of intestinal strongyloidiasis and onchocerciasis (river blindness).	{"indications": ["Indicated for the treatment of intestinal strongyloidiasis caused by Strongyloides stercoralis and onchocerciasis (river blindness) caused by Onchocerca volvulus."], "sideEffects": ["Fever", "Pruritus", "Dizziness and lightheadedness", "Edema", "Rash", "Tender lymphadenopathy", "Perspiration", "Chills", "Myalgia", "Arthralgia", "Facial edema and swelling (Mazzotti reaction)", "Severe orthostatic hypotension accompanied by sweating, tachycardia, and confusion", "Joint pain or synovitis (9.3%)", "Axillary lymph node enlargement and tenderness (10.0% and 4.4% respectively), cervical (5.3% and 1.3%), and inguinal (12.6% and 13.9%)", "Dermatological reactions including edema, papules, pustules, rashes, and urticaria (22.7%)", "Headache (0.2%)", "Myalgia (0.4%)"], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "GABA receptor agonists (such as benzodiazepines and sodium valproate)", "effect": "Theoretically, the medication may potentiate the effects of these agents."}], "effectsOnDriving": "There is currently no data indicating that the medication affects the ability to drive and operate machinery. However, adverse reactions such as headache, dizziness, and hypotension may occur. Therefore, caution should be exercised when driving or operating hazardous machinery.", "contraindications": ["Patients with known hypersensitivity to any component of the medication.", "Patients with conditions associated with blood-brain barrier impairment, such as African trypanosomiasis and meningitis."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Davipharm", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store in a dry place, protected from light, at a temperature not exceeding 30°C", "packaging": "Box of 1 blister x 4 Tablets", "manufacturer": "Davipharm (Vietnam)"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults and children over 5 years of age: Administer a single dose of 0.15 mg/kg. Higher doses increase adverse reactions without improving therapeutic efficacy. Annual retreatment with the above dosage is required to ensure control of Onchocerca volvulus microfilariae. If patients have heavy ocular microfilarial loads, more frequent retreatment (e.g., every 6 months) may be necessary.\\nRecommended dosage guidelines for ivermectin in the treatment of Onchocerca infection (single oral dose based on body weight): 15 - 25 kg: 3 mg; 26 - 44 kg: 6 mg; 45 - 64 kg: 9 mg; 65 - 84 kg: 12 mg; > 85 kg: 0.15 mg/kg.", "missedDose": "[object Object]", "administration": "Administer ivermectin orally with water early in the morning on an empty stomach, or at another time, but avoid food intake within 2 hours before and after administration.", "overdoseManagement": "[object Object]"}, "generalDescription": "Pizar 6mg is an anthelmintic medication containing ivermectin as the active ingredient. In addition to treating onchocerciasis, the medication is highly effective in the treatment of intestinal strongyloidiasis caused by Strongyloides stercoralis.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Cellactose 80, magnesium stearate, croscarmellose sodium.", "activeIngredients": "Ivermectin 6mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "[object Object]", "lactation": "Ivermectin is excreted in breast milk in low concentrations (less than 2% of the administered dose). Safety in newborns has not been established; therefore, the medication should only be administered to nursing mothers when the potential benefits outweigh the risks to the infant.", "pediatric": "Safety and effectiveness in children under 5 years of age have not been established.", "pregnancy": "Ivermectin may be used after the first trimester of pregnancy."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Clinical experience in children under 5 years of age is limited; therefore, use in this age group is not recommended.", "Because ivermectin potentiates GABA, it is theorized to affect the central nervous system in patients with compromised blood-brain barriers (such as in meningitis or Trypanosoma infection).", "When treating onchodermatitis with ivermectin, hyperreactive-type reactions may occur, potentially leading to more severe adverse effects, particularly edema and exacerbation of the condition.", "Keep out of reach of children."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Report any adverse reactions experienced during the use of the medication to your healthcare provider."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:51:26.56	pizar-6mg-tablets-for-helminthiasis-and-onchocerciasis-1-blister-x-4-tablets	112
1748	Tydol Plus 500mg/65mg Tablets for Mild Pain Relief and Fever Reduction (10 Blisters x 10 Tablets)	P10813	\N	\N	Domestic Pharmaceutical Manufacturer	Vietnam	14634.00	12000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250415090825-0-P10813.jpg?versionId=mhCWg.TMvN5239ECvSh27sdFEFFMrBfm	Tydol Plus tablets are indicated for mild-to-moderate pain relief and fever reduction, containing Paracetamol and Caffeine.	{"sideEffects": ["Severe skin reactions such as Stevens-Johnson syndrome, Toxic Epidermal Necrolysis (TEN), Lyell's syndrome, and Acute Generalized Exanthematous Pustulosis (AGEP), which are rare but potentially fatal.", "Skin rashes and other allergic reactions occasionally occur, typically presenting as a rash or urticaria, but occasionally more severe and accompanied by drug-induced fever and mucosal lesions.", "Acetaminophen overdose can lead to severe hepatic injury and occasionally acute renal tubular necrosis.", "Central nervous system: Agitation, dizziness.", "Skin: Rash.", "Gastrointestinal: Nausea, vomiting.", "Hematological: Blood dyscrasias (neutropenia, pancytopenia, leukopenia), anemia.", "Renal: Nephropathy, renal toxicity upon prolonged abuse.", "Hypersensitivity reactions."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Metoclopramide or Domperidone", "effect": "Increases the absorption rate of acetaminophen."}, {"drug": "Colestyramine", "effect": "Decreases the absorption of acetaminophen."}, {"drug": "Coumarin and Indandione Derivatives", "effect": "Long-term, high-dose administration of acetaminophen slightly increases the anticoagulant effect."}, {"drug": "Phenothiazines and Antipyretic Therapy", "effect": "May induce severe hypothermia."}, {"drug": "Alcohol", "effect": "Excessive and chronic alcohol consumption increases the risk of acetaminophen-induced hepatotoxicity."}, {"drug": "Anticonvulsants (including Phenytoin, Barbiturates, Carbamazepine), Isoniazid, and Antitubercular Medications", "effect": "May increase the hepatotoxicity of acetaminophen."}, {"drug": "Probenecid", "effect": "May reduce the elimination of acetaminophen and increase its plasma half-life."}, {"drug": "CYP1A2 Substrates (such as Clozapine) or Inducers/Inhibitors of this Isoenzyme", "effect": "Caffeine has the potential for pharmacokinetic interactions."}], "effectsOnDriving": "Since dizziness may occur, caution should be exercised during activities such as driving, operating machinery, working at heights, and other hazardous tasks.", "pharmacodynamics": {"mechanismOfAction": "Paracetamol acts on the hypothalamic heat-regulating center to cause antipyresis, vasodilation, and increased peripheral blood flow; it inhibits prostaglandin synthesis in the central nervous system. Caffeine acts as a central nervous system stimulant, constricting cerebral blood vessels and enhancing the analgesic potency of paracetamol."}, "pharmacokinetics": {"absorption": "Paracetamol is rapidly and almost completely absorbed from the gastrointestinal tract. Peak plasma concentrations occur 30 to 60 minutes after oral administration. Caffeine is also rapidly and completely absorbed.", "metabolism": "Paracetamol is metabolized primarily in the liver via cytochrome P450 enzyme pathways, forming minor hepatotoxic intermediate metabolites conjugated by hepatic glutathione. Caffeine is metabolized extensively in the liver by oxidation, demethylation, and acetylation.", "elimination": "Paracetamol is excreted primarily in the urine mainly as glucuronide and sulfate conjugates. Caffeine is eliminated principally via urinary excretion of its metabolites, with a plasma half-life of approximately 3 to 7 hours."}, "contraindications": ["Patients with hypersensitivity to any component of the medication.", "Patients with severe hepatic impairment.", "Patients with glucose-6-phosphate dehydrogenase (G6PD) deficiency.", "Children under 12 years of age."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Tydol Plus", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store at temperatures below 30°C, in a dry place, protected from light.", "packaging": "Box of 10 blisters x 10 tablets", "manufacturer": "Domestic Pharmaceutical Manufacturer"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults and children over 12 years: Oral dose of 1 to 2 tablets every 6 hours as symptoms persist. Do not exceed 8 tablets per 24 hours, or as directed by a physician. Note: The dosage provided is for reference only. The specific dosage depends on the patient's physical condition and disease severity. Consult a physician or healthcare professional for an appropriate dosage regimen.", "missedDose": "If a dose is missed, take it as soon as remembered. However, if it is nearly time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and resume the normal dosing schedule. Do not double the dose.", "administration": "Tydol Plus tablets are administered orally.", "overdoseManagement": "Acetaminophen: Symptoms include nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain occurring within 2 to 3 hours after toxic ingestion. Methemoglobinemia leading to cyanosis of the skin, mucous membranes, and nail beds is a characteristic sign of acute p-aminophenol derivative toxicity. Central nervous system stimulation, agitation, and delirium may occur initially, followed by CNS depression, stupor, hypothermia, tachypnea, tachycardia, hypotension, and circulatory failure. Management: Early diagnosis is critical. Gastric lavage should be performed ideally within 4 hours of ingestion. The primary specific antidote is N-acetylcysteine, administered orally or intravenously, most effective if given within 10 hours of ingestion. Methionine may be used as an alternative. Activated charcoal and/or saline cathartics may also reduce absorption. Caffeine: Symptoms include gastrointestinal pain, mild delirium, insomnia, diuresis, dehydration, and fever. Severe symptoms include cardiac arrhythmias and tonic-clonic seizures. Management: Symptomatic and supportive care, gastric emptying, administration of activated charcoal, and anticonvulsants such as diazepam if necessary."}, "generalDescription": "Tydol Plus is an Over-The-Counter (OTC) medication commonly used for mild pain relief and fever reduction. This medication combines two primary active ingredients: Paracetamol, which provides effective analgesic and antipyretic effects, and Caffeine, which acts as an adjuvant to enhance the analgesic efficacy of paracetamol and increases alertness.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Pregelatinized starch, lactose monohydrate, colloidal anhydrous silica, sodium starch glycolate, maize starch, povidone K30, talc, magnesium stearate, Opadry II white, Ponceau 4R lake.", "activeIngredients": "Paracetamol 500mg, Caffeine 65mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Use with caution; dose adjustment may be necessary based on renal and hepatic function.", "lactation": "Caffeine is excreted in breast milk and may cause stimulant effects in nursing infants; therefore, this medication should not be used by nursing mothers.", "pediatric": "Contraindicated in children under 12 years of age.", "pregnancy": "Acetaminophen-caffeine combination is not recommended during pregnancy due to potential risks of low birth weight and spontaneous abortion associated with caffeine."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Physicians should warn patients about signs of serious, potentially fatal skin reactions including Stevens-Johnson syndrome, Toxic Epidermal Necrolysis (TEN), Lyell's syndrome, and Acute Generalized Exanthematous Pustulosis (AGEP).", "Patients must discontinue acetaminophen and seek immediate medical attention upon the first appearance of skin rash or any other sign of hypersensitivity. Patients with a history of hypersensitivity reactions should not use products containing acetaminophen.", "Blood dyscrasias including thrombocytopenia, leukopenia, and pancytopenia have been reported with p-aminophenol derivatives, especially during prolonged use of large doses.", "Exercise caution when administering acetaminophen to patients with preexisting anemia, hepatic impairment, renal impairment, alcoholism, chronic malnutrition, or dehydration.", "Avoid excessive alcohol consumption during treatment due to increased hepatotoxicity risks.", "Avoid excessive caffeine consumption (coffee, tea) while taking this medication.", "This medication contains lactose; patients with rare hereditary problems of galactose intolerance, Lapp lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption should not take this medicine.", "This medication contains Ponceau 4R lake, which may cause allergic reactions."], "adverseReactionManagement": "If adverse effects occur, discontinue use immediately, notify your doctor, or go to the nearest medical facility for prompt management."}	f	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:51:43.705	tydol-plus-500mg-65mg-tablets-for-mild-pain-relief-and-fever-reduction-10-blisters-x-10-tablets	382
1750	Cidetuss 100mg Capsules for Cough, Cold, and Allergic Rhinitis (10 Blisters x 10 Soft Capsules)	P11166	\N	\N	Imexpharm	Vietnam	123457.00	100000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250520065851-0-P11166.png?versionId=VP8Gnjwnua7n.09pGgijLz3FP4VswEOf	Cidetuss 100mg is a combination medication formulated for the relief of coughs due to minor throat and bronchial irritation, expectoration of mucus, symptoms of flu and common cold, and allergic rhinitis.	{"indications": ["Indicated for the treatment of respiratory tract conditions, particularly coughs associated with upper respiratory tract infections, common cold, flu, and allergic rhinitis."], "sideEffects": ["Rare adverse reactions include dizziness, headache, diarrhea, vomiting or nausea, abdominal pain, rash, and urticaria. Nephrolithiasis (kidney stones) has been reported in patients abusing guaifenesin-containing preparations.", "Somnolence (drowsiness) is the most frequent adverse effect, and its incidence is dose-dependent. Additionally, cetirizine may cause fatigue, dry mouth, pharyngitis, dizziness, headache, and nausea. Less frequent effects include anorexia, increased appetite, urinary retention, flushing, and increased salivation.", "Common side effects of dextromethorphan include fatigue, dizziness, tachycardia, and flushing. Urticaria is uncommon, and skin rashes occur rarely. Mild drowsiness or gastrointestinal disturbances may occasionally occur."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Monoamine Oxidase Inhibitors (MAOIs)", "effect": "Contraindicated due to the risk of severe, potentially fatal hypertensive crises and central nervous system excitation."}, {"drug": "Theophylline", "effect": "Slight decrease in the clearance of cetirizine when administered concomitantly."}, {"drug": "Central Nervous System (CNS) Depressants", "effect": "CNS depressant effects may be potentiated when used concurrently with dextromethorphan."}, {"drug": "Enzyme Inhibitors (such as Amiodarone, Haloperidol, Propafenone, Quinidine, and Selective Serotonin Reuptake Inhibitors [SSRIs])", "effect": "Risk of increasing serum concentrations of dextromethorphan, leading to enhanced adverse effects."}, {"drug": "Alcohol", "effect": "Avoid concurrent use due to the risk of increased central nervous system depression and psychomotor impairment."}], "effectsOnDriving": "Avoid administering this medication to patients who drive vehicles or operate machinery, as the product may cause drowsiness, somnolence, and dizziness.", "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity to any of the active ingredients or excipients in this medication.", "Pregnant and lactating women.", "Children under 4 years of age.", "Patients currently receiving Monoamine Oxidase Inhibitors (MAOIs) or within 14 weeks of stopping such treatment."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Imexpharm", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store below 30°C, protect from moisture and light.", "packaging": "Box of 10 blisters x 10 Soft Capsules", "manufacturer": "Imexpharm Corporation (Vietnam)"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults and children aged 6 years and older: Take 1 capsule 2 times daily. Children aged 4 to under 6 years: Take 1 capsule daily. Children under 4 years of age: The dosage form and strength of this medication are not suitable for children under 4 years old. Note: The above dosages are for reference only. The specific dosage depends on the patient's constitution and the severity of the condition. Consult a physician or healthcare professional for an appropriate dosage regimen.", "missedDose": "If you miss a dose of Cidetuss, take it as soon as possible. However, if it is almost time for your next dose, skip the missed dose and resume your regular dosing schedule. Do not double the dose to make up for a forgotten dose.", "administration": "Cidetuss cough capsules are administered orally, before or after meals.", "overdoseManagement": "In the event of a Cidetuss overdose, the potential contribution of each component (guaifenesin, cetirizine, or dextromethorphan) must be evaluated for appropriate management.\\nGuaifenesin: Symptoms: Ingestion of doses higher than therapeutic levels may cause nausea and vomiting. Management: Gastric lavage if detected early, along with symptomatic treatment.\\nCetirizine: Symptoms: The most frequent symptom of cetirizine overdose is somnolence in adults; agitation may occur in children. In severe overdose, induce emesis and perform gastric lavage, alongside supportive measures. There is currently no specific antidote.\\nDextromethorphan: Symptoms: Nausea, vomiting, somnolence, blurred vision, nystagmus, urinary retention, stupor, hallucinations, ataxia, respiratory depression, and convulsions. Management: Supportive care, intravenous administration of naloxone (2 mg), and repeated doses if necessary, up to a total dose of 10 mg."}, "generalDescription": "Cidetuss 100mg is a pharmaceutical preparation utilized for the management and treatment of respiratory conditions, specifically designed to suppress dry or irritative coughs, loosen phlegm and bronchial secretions, and relieve allergic symptoms such as sneezing and rhinorrhea.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Lecithin, Beeswax, Soybean Oil, Gelatin, Glycerin, Vanillin, Titanium Dioxide, L-Lysine HCl, Citric Acid, FD&C Yellow No. 5, FD&C Yellow No. 6, Patent Blue V.", "activeIngredients": "Each soft capsule contains: Guaifenesin 100mg, Cetirizine Dihydrochloride 5mg, Dextromethorphan Hydrobromide 15mg."}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Due to insufficient clinical data regarding the excretion of this medication in breast milk, administration during lactation should be avoided to ensure infant safety. If use is essential, consult a physician to weigh potential benefits against risks.", "pregnancy": "Due to insufficient clinical safety data regarding the use of this medication in pregnant women, administration during pregnancy should be avoided to ensure fetal safety. If use is essential, consult a physician to carefully weigh potential benefits against risks."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Exercise caution when administering the medication to patients with excessive sputum production, prolonged or chronic coughs associated with smoking, asthma, pneumothorax, chronic bronchitis, pulmonary emphysema, or respiratory impairment.", "Dosage adjustment is required in patients with hepatic impairment, moderate-to-severe renal impairment, or patients undergoing hemodialysis.", "Avoid use in patients with porphyria, as guaifenesin has been shown to induce porphyrin metabolism in animal models.", "Use with caution in patients at risk for or experiencing respiratory depression.", "Avoid concomitant use with alcohol and other central nervous system depressants.", "Abuse of guaifenesin-containing products may lead to nephrolithiasis.", "Abuse and dependence on dextromethorphan may occur (though rare), particularly with high-dose use.", "Patients must maintain adequate hydration during treatment. Do not self-administer for more than 7 days without consulting a physician."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:51:50.324	cidetuss-100mg-capsules-for-cough-cold-and-allergic-rhinitis-10-blisters-x-10-soft-capsules	83
