imately 13%."}, {"drug": "Rifampin", "effect": "Decreases the area under the curve (AUC) of etoricoxib by 65%."}, {"drug": "Methotrexate", "effect": "Toxicity monitoring is required when etoricoxib doses exceed 90 mg."}, {"drug": "Angiotensin-Converting Enzyme (ACE) inhibitors", "effect": "May reduce the antihypertensive efficacy."}, {"drug": "Lithium", "effect": "May increase plasma lithium concentrations."}, {"drug": "Aspirin", "effect": "Increases the incidence of gastrointestinal ulceration and other complications."}, {"drug": "Oral contraceptives", "effect": "Increases the AUC of ethinyl estradiol by 50°60%."}], "effectsOnDriving": "No information available.", "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity to any component of the medication.", "Active peptic ulcer disease or gastrointestinal bleeding.", "Severe renal impairment (CrCl < 30 mL/min).", "History of asthma, acute rhinitis, nasal polyps, angioneurotic edema, or urticaria following the administration of aspirin or NSAIDs.", "Pregnancy and lactation.", "Children under 16 years of age.", "Cystitis.", "Hepatic impairment ranging from mild to severe.", "Heart failure.", "Inflammatory bowel disease."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Davipharm", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store in a dry place, protected from light, at a temperature not exceeding 30°C.", "packaging": "Box of 3 blisters x 10 Tablets.", "manufacturer": "Dat Vi Phu Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company (Vietnam)."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Dosage for the treatment of acute gout attacks: 120 mg once daily. The 120 mg dose should be used only during the acute symptomatic period, limited to a maximum of 8 days of treatment. Dosage in patients with hepatic impairment: For mild hepatic impairment (Child-Pugh score 5°6), the maximum dose is 60 mg once daily. For moderate hepatic impairment (Child-Pugh score 7°9), the dose should not exceed 60 mg every other day or 30 mg once daily. Etoricoxib should be avoided in patients with severe hepatic impairment (Child-Pugh score - 10).", "missedDose": "If a dose is missed, take it as soon as possible. However, if it is almost time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and resume the regular dosing schedule. Do not double the dose to make up for a forgotten one.", "administration": "Magrax-F is administered orally.", "overdoseManagement": "No clinical reports of etoricoxib overdose are available. In the event of an overdose, standard supportive measures should be employed, such as removing unabsorbed medication from the gastrointestinal tract, clinical monitoring, and supportive therapy as indicated. Etoricoxib is not dialyzable via hemodialysis."}, "generalDescription": "Magrax-F is manufactured by Dat Vi Phu Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company with Etoricoxib as the active ingredient, serving as a medication used for the treatment of acute gout attacks.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Microcrystalline cellulose, lactose monohydrate, povidone, sodium starch glycolate, sodium lauryl sulfate, magnesium stearate, hydroxypropyl methylcellulose, talc, titanium dioxide, polyethylene glycol 6000, green mint dye, sunset yellow dye, brilliant blue dye... q.s. 1 tablet.", "activeIngredients": "Etoricoxib 120mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Use with caution.", "lactation": "It is unknown whether the medication is excreted in human breast milk. A decision must be made whether to discontinue breastfeeding or discontinue the medication.", "pediatric": "Contraindicated in children under 16 years of age.", "pregnancy": "Avoid use during late pregnancy. Use during the first two trimesters only if the potential benefit outweighs the potential risk to the fetus."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Exercise caution in patients with ischemic heart disease, renal impairment, cirrhosis, left ventricular dysfunction, hypertension, predisposition to fluid retention, elderly patients, dehydrated patients, hyperlipidemia, and diabetes mellitus. When using the high dose of 120 mg/day, treatment duration must not exceed 8 days. Be aware of cardiovascular thrombotic risks (myocardial infarction, stroke). Use the lowest effective dose for the shortest possible duration."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Inform your physician immediately of any adverse reactions experienced during treatment with the medication."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:52:26.547	magrax-f-120mg-tablets-for-acute-gout-attacks-3-blisters-x-10-tablets	112
