1646	Amlor 5mg Tablets for Hypertension and Angina Pectoris (3 Blisters x 10 Tablets)	P00493	\N	\N	Pfizer	According to the manufacturer's specification.	296250.00	237000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20240510103723-0-P00493_1.jpg	Amlor 5mg tablets containing amlodipine, indicated for the treatment of hypertension and coronary artery disease (angina pectoris), manufactured by Pfizer (3 blisters x 10 tablets).	{"indications": ["For the treatment of hypertension and myocardial ischemia (angina pectoris)."], "sideEffects": ["Nervous system disorders: Headache, dizziness, somnolence, hypertonia, hypoesthesia/paresthesia, peripheral neuropathy, syncope, dysgeusia, tremor, extrapyramidal disorder.", "Cardiac disorders: Palpitations, myocardial infarction, cardiac arrhythmias, chest pain.", "Vascular disorders: Flushing, hypotension, vasculitis.", "Gastrointestinal disorders: Abdominal pain, nausea, bowel habit changes, dry mouth, dyspepsia, gingival hyperplasia, pancreatitis, vomiting.", "General disorders and administration site conditions: Edema, fatigue, asthenia, malaise, pain.", "Blood and lymphatic system disorders: Leukopenia, thrombocytopenia.", "Metabolic and nutritional disorders: Hyperglycemia, weight increase/decrease.", "Psychiatric disorders: Insomnia, mood alterations.", "Eye disorders: Visual impairment.", "Ear and labyrinth disorders: Tinnitus.", "Respiratory, thoracic and mediastinal disorders: Cough, dyspnea, rhinitis, epistaxis (in children).", "Skin and subcutaneous tissue disorders: Alopecia, hyperhidrosis, purpura, skin discoloration, urticaria, pruritus, rash, angioedema, erythema multiforme.", "Musculoskeletal and connective tissue disorders: Arthralgia, back pain, muscle spasms, myalgia.", "Renal and urinary disorders: Pollakiuria, micturition disorder, nocturia.", "Reproductive system and breast disorders: Gynecomastia, erectile dysfunction.", "Hepatobiliary disorders: Hepatitis, jaundice, and hepatic enzyme elevations."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Simvastatin", "effect": "Increased exposure to simvastatin; simvastatin dose should be limited to 20 mg daily when co-administered with amlodipine."}, {"drug": "Grapefruit juice", "effect": "May increase bioavailability and the hypotensive effect."}, {"drug": "CYP3A4 inhibitors (Diltiazem, Ketoconazole, Itraconazole, Ritonavir, Clarithromycin)", "effect": "Increased plasma concentrations of amlodipine, elevating the risk of hypotension."}, {"drug": "CYP3A4 inducers (Rifampicin, Hypericum perforatum / St. John's wort)", "effect": "May reduce plasma concentrations of amlodipine."}, {"drug": "Cyclosporine", "effect": "Potential increase in trough blood concentrations of cyclosporine."}, {"drug": "Tacrolimus", "effect": "Risk of increased blood concentrations of tacrolimus."}], "effectsOnDriving": "This medication has negligible influence on the ability to drive and operate machinery.", "contraindications": ["Patients with a known history of hypersensitivity to dihydropyridines, amlodipine, or any of the excipients in this medication."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Pfizer", "origin": "According to the manufacturer's specification.", "storage": "Store below 30°C in a dry place, protected from light. Keep out of reach of children.", "packaging": "Box containing 3 blisters x 10 tablets."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "For hypertension and angina, the usual initial dose is 5 mg of amlodipine once daily, which may be increased to a maximum dose of 10 mg once daily depending on individual patient response. For patients with coronary artery disease, the recommended dose is 5 mg to 10 mg once daily. Pediatric patients aged 6 to 17 years: 2.5 mg to 5 mg once daily.", "missedDose": "Take the missed dose as soon as remembered. If it is almost time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and resume the regular dosing schedule. Do not double doses.", "administration": "Administered orally via tablets.", "overdoseManagement": "Overdose may cause excessive peripheral vasodilation, reflex tachycardia, and severe systemic hypotension. Management: Administer activated charcoal, perform gastric lavage, provide cardiovascular support, continuously monitor cardiac and respiratory function, administer vasopressors, and give intravenous calcium gluconate if necessary. Hemodialysis is not effective."}, "generalDescription": "Amlor 5mg is a medication containing the active ingredient amlodipine, belonging to the class of calcium channel blockers. This medication is manufactured by Pfizer and is primarily used for the treatment of hypertension and angina pectoris.", "detailedIngredients": {"activeIngredients": "Amlodipine 5mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Normal dosage can be used; the medication is generally well tolerated.", "lactation": "Safety during lactation has not been established.", "pediatric": "The recommended antihypertensive dose for pediatric patients aged 6-17 years is 2.5-5 mg daily. Safety and efficacy in children under 6 years of age have not been established.", "pregnancy": "Should only be used during pregnancy if no safer alternative is available and when the underlying disease carries a greater risk to the mother and fetus."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Use in patients with heart failure: May be associated with an increased incidence of pulmonary edema.", "Use in patients with hepatic impairment: Elimination half-life is prolonged; use with caution."], "adverseReactionManagement": "Discontinue use of the medication and notify a physician or seek immediate medical attention if adverse reactions occur."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:47:35.149	amlor-5mg-tablets-for-hypertension-and-angina-pectoris-3-blisters-x-10-tablets	143
1652	Peritol 4mg Cyproheptadine Hydrochloride Tablets for Allergic Conditions and Vascular Headaches (10 Blisters x 10 Tablets)	P01102	\N	\N	\N	Vietnam	158228.00	125000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250508070551-0-P01102.jpg?versionId=ATXxQjN7WQPMIYuSlMQzTzve3Bfp56ki	Peritol 4mg tablets contain cyproheptadine hydrochloride, indicated for the treatment of various allergic conditions, pruritus, and vascular headaches.	{"indications": ["Allergic conditions, particularly those accompanied by pruritus, such as acute and chronic urticaria, angioneurotic edema, drug-induced rashes, pruritus, eczema, eczematoid dermatitis, contact dermatitis, neurodermatitis, allergic rhinitis, vasomotor rhinitis, serum sickness, and insect bites.", "Vascular headaches (migraine, histaminic headache)."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Monoamine oxidase (MAO) inhibitors", "effect": "May potentiate and prolong the anticholinergic effects."}, {"drug": "Alcohol and central nervous system (CNS) depressants", "effect": "Additive central nervous system depression."}, {"drug": "Selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors (SSRIs)", "effect": "May affect the efficacy of the medication, potentially leading to depression relapse."}, {"drug": "Tricyclic antidepressants", "effect": "May cause false-positive results in urine drug screens due to overlapping toxicity and symptom profiles."}], "effectsOnDriving": "May cause dizziness, somnolence, and sedation. Patients should avoid driving or operating machinery upon initiation of therapy and until individual response is established.", "manufacturingInfo": {"storage": "Store in a dry place at temperatures below 30°C."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults: Initial dose of 4-20 mg/day, commonly 12-16 mg/day. Chronic urticaria: 6 mg/day. Acute migraine: 4 mg, may be repeated after 30 minutes, maximum 8 mg over 4-6 hours. Migraine maintenance dose: 12 mg/day. Maximum 32 mg/day. Children over 2 years: 0.25 mg/kg/day or 8 mg/m - . Children aged 2-6 years: 4-6 mg/day (maximum 12 mg). Children aged 7-14 years: 8-12 mg/day (maximum 16 mg).", "administration": "Dosage must be individualized based on patient response. The therapeutic effect of a single dose typically lasts for 4 to 6 hours. It is recommended to administer the first dose after the evening meal.", "overdoseManagement": "Symptoms: Central nervous system depression (somnolence, coma), excitation, seizures, cardiorespiratory arrest, anticholinergic effects. Management: Induction of emesis or gastric lavage, administration of activated charcoal, symptomatic and supportive management of neurological symptoms, management of anticholinergic effects, and treatment of hypotension with vasopressors."}, "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Magnesium stearate, gelatin, talc, potato starch, lactose monohydrate (128 mg)", "activeIngredients": "4 mg cyproheptadine hydrochloride (equivalent to 4.3 mg cyproheptadine hydrochloride sesquihydrate)"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Debilitated elderly patients over 65 years old should avoid use due to increased susceptibility to adverse reactions.", "lactation": "Decide whether to discontinue nursing or discontinue the medication, taking into account the importance of the drug to the mother.", "pediatric": "Contraindicated in children under 2 years of age.", "pregnancy": "Do not use unless the potential benefit outweighs the potential risk to the fetus."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Do not use in acute asthma attacks.", "May diminish alertness or cause paradoxical excitation in young children.", "Contraindicated in children under 2 years of age.", "Use with caution in patients with a history of bronchial asthma, increased intraocular pressure, hyperthyroidism, cardiovascular disease, or hypertension.", "Avoid alcohol consumption while taking this medication.", "Blood counts should be monitored periodically during long-term therapy if signs of hematologic abnormalities occur.", "Contains lactose; should not be used in patients with galactose intolerance, Lapp lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:47:54.447	peritol-4mg-cyproheptadine-hydrochloride-tablets-for-allergic-conditions-and-vascular-headaches-10	\N
1659	Klamentin 500mg/125mg (625mg) Amoxicillin and Clavulanate Potassium Film-Coated Tablets for Bacterial Infections (3 Blisters x 4 Tablets)	P00464	\N	\N	DHG Pharma	Vietnam	79870.00	61500.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250728074601-0-P00464.png?versionId=64yruUSELKgAN8_emsUUKiIiy1mosMcy	Klamentin 500mg/125mg is a combination antibiotic containing Amoxicillin and Clavulanic Acid, indicated for the treatment of various bacterial infections caused by susceptible organisms.	{"sideEffects": ["Skin: Mucocutaneous candidiasis.", "Gastrointestinal: Diarrhea, nausea, vomiting.", "Gastrointestinal: Indigestion (dyspepsia).", "Skin: Rash, pruritus, urticaria.", "Hepatic: Mild elevation in AST and/or ALT.", "Systemic: Anaphylaxis, Stevens-Johnson syndrome.", "Gastrointestinal: Pseudomembranous colitis."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Acenocoumarol or Warfarin", "effect": "Abnormal prolongation of prothrombin time (increased INR) has been reported in patients receiving coumarins concomitantly with amoxicillin. Appropriate monitoring should be undertaken if concurrent administration is necessary."}, {"drug": "Methotrexate", "effect": "Penicillins can reduce the excretion of methotrexate, resulting in a potential increase in toxicity, with increased hematological adverse effects."}, {"drug": "Probenecid", "effect": "Concomitant use of probenecid decreases renal tubular secretion of amoxicillin, resulting in increased and prolonged blood concentrations of amoxicillin."}, {"drug": "Mycophenolate Mofetil", "effect": "In patients receiving mycophenolate mofetil, reduction in pre-dose concentration of the active metabolite mycophenolic acid of approximately 50% has been reported following commencement of oral amoxicillin plus clavulanic acid. Close clinical monitoring is advised."}], "effectsOnDriving": "The medication may cause adverse effects such as dizziness and headache; therefore, caution should be exercised when driving vehicles, operating machinery, working at heights, or performing hazardous tasks.", "pharmacodynamics": {"mechanismOfAction": "Amoxicillin is a semisynthetic antibiotic with a broad spectrum of bactericidal activity against many Gram-positive and Gram-negative microorganisms. It acts by inhibiting bacterial cell wall synthesis. Clavulanic Acid possesses a similar beta-lactam structure to penicillins and has the ability to inactivate a wide variety of beta-lactamase enzymes commonly found in microorganisms resistant to penicillins and cephalosporins."}, "pharmacokinetics": {"absorption": "Both amoxicillin and clavulanic acid are fully dissociated in aqueous solution at physiological pH. Both components are rapidly and well absorbed orally when taken at the start of a meal.", "metabolism": "Amoxicillin is partly excreted in the urine as inactive penicilloic acid. Clavulanic acid is extensively metabolized in man to 2,5-dihydro-4-(2-hydroxyethyl)-5-oxo-1H-pyrrole-3-carboxylic acid and 1-amino-4-hydroxybutan-2-one and eliminated in urine and feces as well as in carbon dioxide in expired air."}, "contraindications": ["Patients with a history of hypersensitivity to penicillins, cephalosporins, or any beta-lactam antibacterial agents, or to any of the excipients.", "Patients with a history of jaundice or hepatic dysfunction associated with amoxicillin/clavulanic acid."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "DHG Pharma", "origin": "Vietnam", "storage": "Store in a dry place, at temperatures not exceeding 30°C, protect from light.", "packaging": "Box of 3 blisters x 4 Tablets", "manufacturer": "DHG Pharmaceutical Joint Stock Company (Vietnam)"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Dosage depends on the expected pathogens and their susceptibility to antibacterial agents, the severity and site of infection, and the age, weight, and renal function of the patient.\\nFor adults and pediatric patients - 40 kg: 500 mg / 125 mg 3 times daily. Total daily dose is 1500 mg amoxicillin / 375 mg clavulanic acid.\\nFor pediatric patients < 40 kg: 20 mg/5 mg/kg/day to 60 mg/15 mg/kg/day divided in 3 doses. Maximum daily dose does not exceed 2400 mg amoxicillin / 500 mg clavulanic acid. No dosage recommendation is available for children < 2 years old.\\nRenal impairment: Adjust dosage based on the maximum recommended level of amoxicillin. No adjustment is required in patients with creatinine clearance (CrCl) > 30 mL/min.\\nAdults and pediatric patients - 40 kg:\\n- CrCl 10 to 30 mL/min: 500 mg / 125 mg twice daily.\\n- CrCl < 10 mL/min: 500 mg / 125 mg once daily.\\n- Hemodialysis: 500 mg / 125 mg every 24 hours, plus 500 mg / 125 mg during dialysis, repeated at the end of dialysis (due to decreased serum concentrations of amoxicillin and clavulanic acid).\\nPediatric patients < 40 kg:\\n- CrCl 10 to 30 mL/min: 15 mg / 3.75 mg/kg twice daily (Max 500 mg / 125 mg twice daily).\\n- CrCl < 10 mL/min: Single dose of 15 mg / 3.75 mg/kg/day (Max 500 mg / 125 mg).\\n- Hemodialysis: 15 mg / 3.75 mg/kg once daily. Prior to hemodialysis: 15 mg / 3.75 mg/kg. To restore circulating drug levels, administer 15 mg / 3.75 mg/kg after hemodialysis.\\nHepatic impairment: Use with caution and monitor hepatic function at regular intervals. Data are insufficient to recommend a specific dosage.\\nDuration of treatment should be determined by the patient's response. Certain infections (e.g., osteomyelitis) require prolonged treatment. Treatment should not exceed 14 days without a medical review.", "missedDose": "If a dose is missed, take it as soon as remembered. However, if it is almost time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and resume the regular dosing schedule. Do not double the dose to make up for a forgotten dose.", "administration": "Swallow Klamentin tablets whole without chewing. If necessary, tablets may be broken in half and swallowed without chewing. Use within 30 days after opening the blister pouch. Administer at the start of meals to minimize gastrointestinal intolerance and optimize the absorption of amoxicillin/clavulanic acid. Treatment may be initiated with intravenous therapy and continued with oral therapy, or as directed by a physician.", "overdoseManagement": "Symptoms: Gastrointestinal symptoms and disturbance of fluid and electrolyte balances may be evident. Amoxicillin crystalluria, in some cases leading to renal failure, has been observed. Convulsions may occur in patients with impaired renal function or those receiving high doses.\\nManagement: Symptomatic treatment of gastrointestinal manifestations with attention to fluid and electrolyte balance. Amoxicillin/clavulanic acid can be removed from the circulation by hemodialysis."}, "generalDescription": "Klamentin 500mg/125mg Tablets is a combination medication containing two active ingredients: Amoxicillin (a penicillin-class antibiotic) and Clavulanic Acid (a beta-lactamase inhibitor). It is used as an antimicrobial agent to treat various infections caused by susceptible bacteria that may lead to significant health complications.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Aerosil, Crospovidone (Polyplasdon XL), Microcrystalline cellulose (Avicel M112), Magnesium stearate, Sepifilm LP914, Titanium dioxide, Talc", "activeIngredients": "Amoxicillin (as Amoxicillin Trihydrate) 500mg, Clavulanic Acid (as Potassium Clavulanate) 125mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "[object Object]", "lactation": "Both substances are excreted in breast milk (minus quantities of clavulanic acid). Consequently, diarrhea and fungus infection of the mucous membranes are possible in the nursing infant, so that nursing might have to be discontinued. Amoxicillin/clavulanic acid should only be used during lactation after benefit-risk assessment by the physician.", "pediatric": "[object Object]", "pregnancy": "Animal studies do not indicate direct or indirect harmful effects with respect to pregnancy, embryonal/fetal development, parturition, or postnatal development. Human data from a single study in women with preterm premature rupture of the membranes indicated that prophylactic treatment with amoxicillin/clavulanic acid may be associated with an increased risk of necrotizing enterocolitis in neonates. Use should be avoided unless considered essential by the physician."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Careful inquiry should be made concerning previous hypersensitivity reactions to penicillins, cephalosporins, or other allergens prior to initiating therapy with amoxicillin/clavulanic acid.", "Where an infection is proven to be due to an amoxicillin-susceptible organism, consideration should be given to switching from amoxicillin/clavulanic acid to amoxicillin in accordance with official guidance.", "Klamentin is not suitable for use when there is a high risk that the presumed pathogens have reduced susceptibility or resistance to beta-lactams not mediated by beta-lactamases susceptible to clavulanic acid. It should not be used to treat penicillin-resistant S. pneumoniae.", "Convulsions may occur in patients with impaired renal function or in those receiving high doses.", "Avoid using amoxicillin/clavulanic acid if infectious mononucleosis is suspected, as the occurrence of a morbilliform rash has been associated with this condition following the use of amoxicillin.", "Concomitant use of allopurinol during treatment with amoxicillin can increase the likelihood of allergic skin reactions.", "Prolonged treatment may occasionally result in overgrowth of non-susceptible organisms. Discontinue use and institute appropriate therapy if superinfections occur.", "Exercise caution when administering amoxicillin/clavulanic acid to patients with evidence of hepatic impairment.", "Antibiotic-associated colitis has been reported, ranging in severity from mild to life-threatening.", "In renal impairment, dosage should be adjusted according to the degree of impairment. Adequate fluid intake and urinary output should be maintained during administration of high doses of amoxicillin to reduce the possibility of amoxicillin crystalluria.", "When testing for glucose in urine during amoxicillin treatment, enzymatic glucose oxidase methods should be used, as non-enzymatic methods may yield false-positive results. Positive results with the Bio-Rad Laboratories Platelia Aspergillus EIA test have been reported."], "adverseReactionManagement": "If an allergic reaction occurs (e.g., rash, angioedema, anaphylaxis, Stevens-Johnson syndrome), discontinue amoxicillin therapy immediately and initiate emergency treatment with adrenaline, oxygen, intravenous corticosteroids, and airway management including intubation. Never administer penicillins or cephalosporins again.\\nPseudomembranous colitis: If mild, discontinue medication. If severe (likely due to Clostridium difficile), administer fluid and electrolyte replacement, and anti-clostridial antibiotics (e.g., oral metronidazole or vancomycin)."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:48:17.768	klamentin-500mg-125mg-625mg-amoxicillin-and-clavulanate-potassium-film-coated-tablets-for-bacterial	62
1717	Cavinton Forte 10mg Vinpocetine Tablets for Cerebral Circulatory Disorders and Hearing Impairment (2 Blisters x 15 Tablets)	P02183	\N	\N	Gedeon Richter Plc.	Hungary	181111.00	163000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/P02183_1_l.jpg	Cavinton Forte 10mg tablets by Gedeon Richter indicated for the treatment of cerebral circulatory disorders and hearing impairment (2 blisters x 15 tablets).	{"sideEffects": ["Common: nausea, dry mouth, abdominal discomfort, flushing, hypotension, headache, dizziness, vertigo, somnolence, euphoria.", "Rare: decreased platelet count, anterior chamber hemorrhage, cardiac arrhythmias (tachycardia or bradycardia, prolonged QT interval), palpitations, dyspepsia, abdominal pain, constipation, diarrhea, vomiting, asthenia, hypoglycemia, blood urea increased, anorexia, dysgeusia, psychomotor hyperactivity, sleep disorders, insomnia, agitation, restlessness, pruritus, hyperhidrosis, urticaria, rash, hypertension, flushing episodes."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Alpha-methyldopa", "effect": "Slight additive hypotensive effect may occur."}, {"drug": "Central nervous system-active medications, anticoagulants, and antiarrhythmic medications", "effect": "Caution is advised when administered concomitantly."}], "effectsOnDriving": "Adverse reactions such as headache, dizziness, vertigo, somnolence, cardiac arrhythmias, psychomotor reactions, agitation, and restlessness may impair the ability to drive and operate machinery.", "contraindications": ["Pregnancy", "Lactation", "Hypersensitivity to vinpocetine or any of the excipients of the medication", "Patients with hereditary galactose intolerance, total lactase deficiency, or glucose-galactose malabsorption"], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Gedeon Richter", "origin": "Hungary", "storage": "Store at temperatures below 30°C, protected from moisture and light. Do not use the medication after the expiration date printed on the packaging.", "packaging": "Box of 2 blisters x 15 tablets", "manufacturer": "Gedeon Richter Plc."}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Use the medication strictly as prescribed by a physician. In the absence of a prescription, the standard recommended dosage is 3 tablets daily, divided into 3 doses.", "administration": "Take the medication orally after meals."}, "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "Colloidal anhydrous silica, magnesium stearate, talc, maize starch, lactose monohydrate", "activeIngredients": "Vinpocetine 10mg"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"lactation": "Contraindicated.", "pregnancy": "Contraindicated."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["Patients with lactose intolerance should note that each tablet contains 83 mg of lactose.", "Inform your physician if you have any other medical conditions (especially heart failure or electrocardiographic abnormalities).", "Electrocardiographic monitoring is recommended in cases of long QT syndrome or when administered concomitantly with medications that prolong the QT interval."]}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:50:02.848	cavinton-forte-10mg-vinpocetine-tablets-for-cerebral-circulatory-disorders-and-hearing-impairment-2	272
1736	Clopalvix 75mg Tablets for Atherosclerotic Thrombotic Events and Vascular Occlusion (5 Blisters x 14 Tablets)	P02709	\N	\N	\N	[object Object]	432584.00	385000.00	https://prod-cdn.pharmacity.io/e-com/images/ecommerce/20250728082923-0-P02709.png?versionId=pAzSGv_OibvlHZyY3C4yHnsv3_9EAZFJ	Clopalvix 75mg is an antiplatelet medication containing Clopidogrel indicated for the prevention of atherothrombotic events and vascular occlusion.	{"indications": ["Recent myocardial infarction (from a few days up to less than 35 days), recent ischemic stroke (from 7 days up to less than 6 months), or established peripheral arterial disease.", "Acute coronary syndrome without ST-segment elevation (unstable angina or non-Q-wave myocardial infarction), including patients undergoing percutaneous coronary intervention, in combination with aspirin.", "Acute myocardial infarction with ST-segment elevation: In combination with aspirin in medical treatment for thrombolytic therapy.", "In patients with atrial fibrillation who are unsuited for treatment with vitamin K antagonists and who have low bleeding risk, clopidogrel is co-administered with aspirin for the prevention of atherothrombotic and thromboembolic events, including stroke."], "sideEffects": ["Bleeding: Gastrointestinal hemorrhage (2.0%), intracranial hemorrhage (0.4%), purpura, bruising, hematoma, and epistaxis. Less frequently reported events include hematuria, eye hemorrhage (mainly conjunctival).", "Hematological: Neutropenia, thrombocytopenia.", "Central and peripheral nervous system: Headache, dizziness, vertigo.", "Gastrointestinal system: Abdominal pain, dyspepsia, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, constipation, gastritis.", "Skin: Rash, pruritus."], "drugInteractions": [{"drug": "Aspirin", "effect": "Aspirin did not modify the ADP-induced platelet aggregation inhibited by clopidogrel, but clopidogrel potentiated the effect of aspirin on collagen-induced platelet aggregation. However, concomitant administration of 500 mg of aspirin twice a day for 1 day did not significantly increase the prolongation of bleeding time induced by clopidogrel. Pharmacodynamic interaction between clopidogrel and aspirin is possible, leading to an increased risk of bleeding. Therefore, caution should be exercised with concomitant use."}, {"drug": "Non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs)", "effect": "In a clinical study involving healthy volunteers, the concomitant administration of naproxen and clopidogrel was associated with increased occult gastrointestinal blood loss. Caution should be used when co-administering NSAIDs with clopidogrel."}, {"drug": "Warfarin", "effect": "Because the co-administration of warfarin with clopidogrel may increase the risk of bleeding, caution should be exercised when combining these medications."}, {"drug": "Heparin", "effect": "In a clinical study in healthy subjects, clopidogrel did not necessitate modification of the heparin dose or alter the effect of heparin on coagulation. Co-administration of heparin had no effect on the inhibition of platelet aggregation induced by clopidogrel. Pharmacodynamic interaction between clopidogrel and heparin is possible, leading to an increased risk of bleeding. Therefore, caution is warranted with concomitant use."}, {"drug": "Thrombolytic agents", "effect": "The safety of the combination of clopidogrel and thrombolytic agents has not been officially established; therefore, caution should be exercised when combining these agents."}, {"drug": "Atenolol, nifedipine, or both atenolol and nifedipine", "effect": "There were no clinically significant pharmacodynamic interactions when clopidogrel was co-administered with atenolol, nifedipine, or both."}, {"drug": "Phenobarbital, cimetidine, or estrogen", "effect": "The pharmacodynamic activity of clopidogrel was not significantly influenced by the co-administration of phenobarbital, cimetidine, or estrogen."}, {"drug": "Digoxin or theophylline", "effect": "The pharmacokinetics of digoxin or theophylline were not modified by the co-administration of clopidogrel."}], "effectsOnDriving": "Caution should be exercised when driving vehicles and operating machinery.", "pharmacodynamics": {"mechanismOfAction": "Clopidogrel selectively inhibits the binding of adenosine diphosphate (ADP) to its platelet receptor and the subsequent ADP-mediated activation of the glycoprotein GPIIb/IIIa complex, thereby inhibiting platelet aggregation. Clopidogrel also inhibits platelet aggregation induced by agonists other than ADP by blocking the amplification of platelet activation by released ADP. Clopidogrel acts by irreversible modification of the platelet ADP receptor. Consequently, platelets exposed to clopidogrel are affected for the remainder of their lifespan.", "pharmacologicalClass": "Thienopyridine antiplatelet agent"}, "pharmacokinetics": {"absorption": "Clopidogrel is rapidly but incompletely absorbed after oral administration, with at least 50% of the dose absorbed.", "metabolism": "Clopidogrel is a prodrug and is extensively metabolized in the liver into its inactive carboxylic acid derivative.", "elimination": "Clopidogrel and its carboxylic acid derivative are highly bound to plasma proteins. Clopidogrel and its metabolites are eliminated via urine and feces, with approximately 50% of the oral dose recovered in urine and 46% in feces over a 5-day period."}, "contraindications": ["Hypersensitivity to clopidogrel or any component of the medication.", "Severe hepatic impairment.", "Active pathological bleeding such as peptic ulcer or intracranial hemorrhage, or any other condition causing severe bleeding.", "Breastfeeding women."], "manufacturingInfo": {"brand": "Clopalvix", "origin": "[object Object]", "storage": "Store in a dry place, below 30°C, protected from light.", "packaging": "[object Object]", "manufacturer": "[object Object]"}, "usageInstructions": {"dosage": "Adults and elderly: 75 mg once daily. Pediatric patients: There is no clinical experience in children; therefore, the medication is not recommended for pediatric use. Patients with acute coronary syndrome: Non-ST-segment elevation acute coronary syndrome (unstable angina or non-Q-wave myocardial infarction): Initiate medical treatment with a single 300 mg loading dose of clopidogrel on day one, followed by 75 mg once daily thereafter. Combined with aspirin 75 - 325 mg daily starting on subsequent days (aspirin doses under 100 mg daily are generally recommended). Acute myocardial infarction with ST-segment elevation: 75 mg once daily, initiated with a 300 mg loading dose in combination with aspirin, with or without thrombolytics. In patients over 75 years of age, treatment should be initiated without a loading dose of 300 mg. Treatment should be continued for at least 4 weeks. Atrial fibrillation: 75 mg once daily, administered in combination with aspirin (75 - 100 mg daily). Note: The above dosages are for reference only. The specific dosage depends on the patient's physical condition and disease severity. Consult a physician or healthcare professional for appropriate dosing.", "missedDose": "If a dose is missed, take it as soon as remembered. However, if it is almost time for the next dose, skip the missed dose and resume the regular dosing schedule. Do not double the dose to make up for a forgotten one.", "administration": "Clopalvix is administered orally and can be taken with or without food.", "overdoseManagement": "Overdose of clopidogrel can lead to prolonged bleeding time and subsequent hemorrhagic complications. Symptoms may include dyspnea, fatigue, prolonged bleeding, gastrointestinal bleeding, and vomiting; appropriate therapy should be instituted if bleeding occurs. There is no known antidotal pharmacological activity reversal for clopidogrel. Platelet transfusion may be used to reverse the pharmacological effects of clopidogrel."}, "generalDescription": "Clopidogrel is a thienopyridine antiplatelet inhibitor structurally and pharmacologically related to ticlopidine. Clopidogrel selectively inhibits the binding of adenosine diphosphate (ADP) to its platelet receptor and the subsequent ADP-mediated activation of the glycoprotein GPIIb/IIIa complex, thereby inhibiting platelet aggregation. Clopidogrel also inhibits platelet aggregation induced by agonists other than ADP by blocking the amplification of platelet activation by released ADP. Clopidogrel acts by irreversible modification of the platelet ADP receptor. Consequently, platelets exposed to clopidogrel are affected for the remainder of their lifespan.", "detailedIngredients": {"excipients": "75mg", "activeIngredients": "Clopidogrel"}, "specialPatientGroups": {"geriatric": "Administer 75 mg once daily. For patients over 75 years of age, initiate treatment with a daily dose of 75 mg without a loading dose.", "lactation": "Contraindicated in breastfeeding women.", "pediatric": "There is no clinical experience with this medication in children. The medication is not recommended for pediatric use.", "pregnancy": "There are no adequate and well-controlled studies in pregnant women. Clopidogrel should be used during pregnancy only if clearly needed."}, "warningsAndPrecautions": ["In patients with acute myocardial infarction, treatment with clopidogrel should not be initiated within the first few days following myocardial infarction.", "Clopidogrel prolongs bleeding time and should be used with caution in patients who may be at risk of increased bleeding from trauma, surgery, or other pathological conditions (particularly gastrointestinal and intraocular).", "Clopidogrel should be used with caution in patients with lesions prone to bleeding (such as ulcers).", "If a patient is scheduled to undergo elective surgery and antiplatelet effect is temporarily not desired, clopidogrel should be discontinued 5 to 7 days prior to surgery.", "There is limited clinical experience with clopidogrel in patients with hepatic and renal impairment; therefore, caution should be exercised when administering the medication to these patient populations.", "Patients must be informed that when taking clopidogrel for an extended duration, they should stop the medication if abnormal bleeding occurs and report any unusual bleeding to their physician.", "Patients should inform physicians and dentists that they are taking clopidogrel before any scheduled surgery and prior to taking any new medication."], "adverseReactionManagement": "If any adverse reactions occur, discontinue use and inform a physician or report to the nearest medical facility for prompt management."}	t	ACTIVE	2026-04-08 21:51:02.528	clopalvix-75mg-tablets-for-atherosclerotic-thrombotic-events-and-vascular-occlusion-5-blisters-x-14	\N
